2. Keeping the upper arms stationary, lower the bar by allowing the elbows to flex. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Pause once the bar is directly above the forehead.
3. Lift the bar back to the starting position by extending the elbow and exhaling; repeat.', '["triceps"]', '["forearms"]', '["ez_bar"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'ez-bar-skullcrusher', 'strength', 'elbow_extension', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Reduce range if you feel elbow pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'EZ-Bar_Skullcrusher', 'EZ-Bar Skullcrusher', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=EZ-Bar+Skull+Crusher+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/EZ-Bar_Skullcrusher.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000013'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
