2. Build up to a brisk walking pace.
3. Stand tall with relaxed shoulders and let your arms swing naturally.
4. Ease down to a walk for a few minutes to cool down.', '["forearms"]', '["abs","glutes","hamstrings","lower_back","quads","traps"]', '["other"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'farmer-s-carry', 'strength', 'carry', 'distance_weight', 'gym', 'compound', NULL, 'bilateral', 'Set weights down with a neutral spine.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Farmers_Walk', 'Farmer''s Walk', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Farmer%27s+Walk+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:specific', 1, '["no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image","no_relations","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-00000000001e'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000002', 'global', NULL, 'Front Barbell Squat', 'front barbell squat', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a barbell that mainly works the quads, with the calves and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, bring your arms up under the bar while keeping the elbows high and the upper arm slightly above parallel to the floor. Rest the bar on top of the deltoids and cross your arms while grasping the bar for total control.
2. Lift the bar off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.
3. Step away from the rack and position your legs using a shoulder width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up at all times as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back.
4. Begin to slowly lower the bar by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calves becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to the floor). Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. If your knees are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor mainly with the middle of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the starting position.
6. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["quads"]', '["calves","glutes","hamstrings"]', '["barbell"]', 'advanced', 'active', 'front-squat-barbell', 'strength', 'squat', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use safety pins/spotter for heavy barbell work; stop if you feel knee or back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Front_Barbell_Squat', 'Front Barbell Squat', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Front+Barbell+Squat+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Front_Barbell_Squat.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","long_step"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000002'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000020', 'global', NULL, 'Goblet Squat', 'goblet squat', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a kettlebell that mainly works the quads, with the calves and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Stand holding a light kettlebell by the horns close to your chest. This will be your starting position.
2. Squat down between your legs until your hamstrings are on your calves. Keep your chest and head up and your back straight.
3. At the bottom position, pause and use your elbows to push your knees out. Return to the starting position, and repeat for 10-20 repetitions.', '["quads"]', '["calves","glutes","hamstrings","front_delts"]', '["kettlebell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'goblet-squat', 'strength', 'squat', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use safety pins/spotter for heavy barbell work; stop if you feel knee or back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Goblet_Squat', 'Goblet Squat', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Goblet+Squat+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Goblet_Squat.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:specific', 0, '["no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000020'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000006', 'global', NULL, 'Incline Dumbbell Press', 'incline dumbbell press', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the chest, with the front delts and triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lie back on an incline bench with a dumbbell in each hand atop your thighs. The palms of your hands will be facing each other.
2. Then, using your thighs to help push the dumbbells up, lift the dumbbells one at a time so that you can hold them at shoulder width.
3. Once you have the dumbbells raised to shoulder width, rotate your wrists forward so that the palms of your hands are facing away from you. This will be your starting position. Be sure to keep full control of the dumbbells at all times. Then breathe out and push the dumbbells up with your chest.
4. Lock your arms at the top, hold for a second, and then start slowly lowering the weight.
5. Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
6. When you are done, place the dumbbells back on your thighs and then on the floor. This is the safest manner to release the dumbbells.', '["chest"]', '["front_delts","triceps"]', '["dumbbell","bench"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'incline-dumbbell-press', 'strength', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Incline_Dumbbell_Press', 'Incline Dumbbell Press', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Incline+Dumbbell+Press+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Press.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000006'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000018', 'global', NULL, 'Leg Extension', 'leg extension', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using the machine that mainly works the quads.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. First choose your weight and sit on the machine with your legs under the pad (feet pointed forward) and the hands holding the side bars. This will be your starting position. Also, make sure that your legs form a 90-degree angle between the lower and upper leg. If the angle is less than 90-degrees then that means the knee is over the toes which in turn creates undue stress at the knee joint. If the machine is designed that way, either look for another machine or just make sure that when you start executing the exercise you stop going down once you hit the 90-degree angle.
2. Using your quadriceps, extend your legs to the maximum as you exhale. Ensure that the rest of the body remains stationary on the seat. Pause a second on the contracted position.
3. Slowly lower the weight back to the original position as you inhale, ensuring that you do not go past the 90-degree angle limit.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of times.', '["quads"]', '[]', '["machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'leg-extensions', 'strength', 'knee_extension', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Adjust the pad to sit just above the ankle.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Leg_Extensions', 'Leg Extensions', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Leg+Extension+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Leg_Extensions.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_relations"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000018'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000016', 'global', NULL, 'Leg Press', 'leg press', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using the machine that mainly works the quads, with the calves and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lower the safety bars holding the weighted platform in place and press the platform all the way up until your legs are fully extended in front of you. Your torso and the legs should make a perfect 90-degree angle. This will be your starting position.
2. As you inhale, slowly lower the platform until your upper and lower legs make a 90-degree angle.
3. Pushing mainly with the heels of your feet and using the quadriceps go back to the starting position as you exhale.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and ensure to lock the safety pins properly once you are done. You do not want that platform falling on you fully loaded.', '["quads"]', '["calves","glutes","hamstrings"]', '["machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'leg-press', 'strength', 'squat', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use safety pins/spotter for heavy barbell work; stop if you feel knee or back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Leg_Press', 'Leg Press', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Leg+Press+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Leg_Press.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:specific', 0, '[]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000016'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000017', 'global', NULL, 'Lying Leg Curl', 'lying leg curl', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using the machine that mainly works the hamstrings.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lie face down on the leg curl machine with the pad just above your heels.
2. Hold the handles and keep your hips still.
3. Curl your heels toward your glutes as far as you can.
4. Lower slowly until your knees are almost straight.', '["hamstrings"]', '[]', '["machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'lying-leg-curls', 'strength', 'knee_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Set the pad just above the heels.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Lying_Leg_Curls', 'Lying Leg Curls', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Lying+Leg+Curl+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_relations","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000017'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
