2. Hold the dumbbell with your arms straight below your shoulders.
3. Row the dumbbell toward your lower ribs, driving your elbows back.
4. Lower the dumbbell slowly to straight arms.
5. Finish all reps on one side, then switch sides and repeat.', '["upper_back"]', '["biceps","lats","front_delts"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'one-arm-dumbbell-row', 'strength', 'horizontal_pull', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'pull', 'unilateral', 'Keep a neutral spine, especially in bent-over rows.', 'free_exercise_db', 'One-Arm_Dumbbell_Row', 'One-Arm Dumbbell Row', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Single-Arm+Dumbbell+Row+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:specific', 1, '["no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-00000000000f'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e1000001-0000-4000-8000-00000000001f', 'global', NULL, 'Single-Arm Kettlebell Swing', 'single-arm kettlebell swing', 'free_exercise_db', 'A single-side compound strength exercise with a kettlebell that mainly works the hamstrings, with the calves and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:fitbud_curated', '1. Stand with your feet a little wider than your hips and the kettlebell a foot in front of you.
2. Hinge and grip the handle with one hand, then hike it back between your legs.
3. Snap your hips forward to swing the kettlebell to chest height with a straight arm.
4. Let it swing back between your legs as you hinge and go straight into the next rep.
5. Finish all reps on one side, then switch sides and repeat.', '["hamstrings"]', '["calves","glutes","lower_back","front_delts"]', '["kettlebell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'one-arm-kettlebell-swings', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'pull', 'unilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'One-Arm_Kettlebell_Swings', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Swings', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Single-Arm+Kettlebell+Swing+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud"}', 1, 'ai_authored:specific', 1, '["ai_authored_steps","csv_disagrees","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-00000000001f'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000015', 'global', NULL, 'Split Squat with Dumbbells', 'split squat with dumbbells', 'free_exercise_db', 'A single-side compound strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the quads, with the glutes and hamstrings assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Position yourself into a staggered stance with the rear foot elevated and front foot forward.
2. Hold a dumbbell in each hand, letting them hang at the sides. This will be your starting position.
3. Begin by descending, flexing your knee and hip to lower your body down. Maintain good posture througout the movement. Keep the front knee in line with the foot as you perform the exercise.
4. At the bottom of the movement, drive through the heel to extend the knee and hip to return to the starting position.
5. Finish all reps on one side, then switch sides and repeat.', '["quads"]', '["glutes","hamstrings"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'split-squat-with-dumbbell', 'strength', 'lunge', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'push', 'unilateral', 'Hold a support for balance if needed; keep loads light until balance is solid.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Split_Squat_with_Dumbbells', 'Split Squat with Dumbbells', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Split+Squat+with+Dumbbells+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Split_Squat_with_Dumbbells.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000015'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000019', 'global', NULL, 'Standing Calf Raise', 'standing calf raise', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using the machine that mainly works the calves.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Adjust the padded lever of the calf raise machine to fit your height.
2. Place your shoulders under the pads provided and position your toes facing forward (or using any of the two other positions described at the beginning of the chapter). The balls of your feet should be secured on top of the calf block with the heels extending off it. Push the lever up by extending your hips and knees until your torso is standing erect. The knees should be kept with a slight bend; never locked. Toes should be facing forward, outwards or inwards as described at the beginning of the chapter. This will be your starting position.
3. Raise your heels as you breathe out by extending your ankles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the knee is kept stationary at all times. There should be no bending at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down.
4. Go back slowly to the starting position as you breathe in by lowering your heels as you bend the ankles until calves are stretched.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["calves"]', '[]', '["machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'standing-calf-raises', 'strength', 'calf_raise', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Hold a support for balance.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Standing_Calf_Raises', 'Standing Calf Raises', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Standing+Calf+Raise+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Standing_Calf_Raises.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","long_step"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000019'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
