2. Hold the barbell at shoulder height.
3. Brace your core and press the barbell straight overhead until your arms are straight.
4. Lower the barbell under control back to shoulder height.', '["front_delts"]', '["triceps"]', '["barbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'overhead-press-barbell', 'strength', 'vertical_push', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Avoid if overhead pressing causes shoulder pain; use a landmine press instead.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Standing_Military_Press', 'Standing Military Press', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Standing+Military+Press+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:specific', 1, '["no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000008'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
