2. Most treadmills have a manual setting, or you can select a program to run.
3. Elevation can be adjusted to change the intensity of the workout.
4. When walking, you should move at a moderate to fast pace, not a leisurely one.
5. Maintain proper posture as you walk, and only hold onto the handles when necessary, such as when dismounting or checking your heart rate.', '["quads"]', '["calves","glutes","hamstrings"]', '["machine","treadmill"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'treadmill-walk', 'cardio', 'locomotion', 'distance_time', 'cardio', 'compound', NULL, 'bilateral', 'Stop if you feel chest pain, dizziness or unusual breathlessness.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Walking_Treadmill', 'Walking, Treadmill', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Treadmill+Walk+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Walking_Treadmill.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:specific', 1, '["few_steps","long_step","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000023'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000012', 'global', NULL, 'Triceps Pushdown', 'triceps pushdown', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the triceps.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Attach a straight or angled bar to a high pulley and grab with an overhand grip (palms facing down) at shoulder width.
2. Standing upright with the torso straight and a very small inclination forward, bring the upper arms close to your body and perpendicular to the floor. The forearms should be pointing up towards the pulley as they hold the bar. This is your starting position.
3. Using the triceps, bring the bar down until it touches the front of your thighs and the arms are fully extended perpendicular to the floor. The upper arms should always remain stationary next to your torso and only the forearms should move. Exhale as you perform this movement.
4. After a second hold at the contracted position, bring the bar slowly up to the starting point. Breathe in as you perform this step.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["triceps"]', '[]', '["cable"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'triceps-pushdown-cable', 'strength', 'elbow_extension', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Reduce range if you feel elbow pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Triceps_Pushdown', 'Triceps Pushdown', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Triceps+Pushdown+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Triceps_Pushdown.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:specific', 0, '[]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000012'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
