2. At the same time, begin to lift the legs up as you crunch your upper torso. Breathe out as you perform this movement. Concentrate on using your abs to move the weight while relaxing your legs and feet.
3. After a second pause, slowly return to the starting position as you breathe in.
4. Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["machine"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'ab-crunch-machine', 'strength', 'core_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Skip or modify if it aggravates lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Ab_Crunch_Machine', 'Ab Crunch Machine', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Ab+Crunch+Machine+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Ab_Crunch_Machine.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'ca17631a-c08e-5283-bca2-a7e97c267c05'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('bfd9d15c-803e-56e4-a858-c80a65b7ec6a', 'global', NULL, 'Ab Roller', 'ab roller', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the abs, with the front delts assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Hold the Ab Roller with both hands and kneel on the floor.
2. Now place the ab roller on the floor in front of you so that you are on all your hands and knees (as in a kneeling push up position). This will be your starting position.
3. Slowly roll the ab roller straight forward, stretching your body into a straight position. Breathe in during this portion of the movement.
4. After a pause at the stretched position, start pulling yourself back to the starting position as you breathe out.', '["abs"]', '["front_delts"]', '["other"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'ab-roller', 'strength', 'core_anti_extension', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Stop when form breaks rather than chasing time.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Ab_Roller', 'Ab Roller', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Ab+Roller+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Ab_Roller.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'bfd9d15c-803e-56e4-a858-c80a65b7ec6a'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('95171473-ba6a-5e73-ac0d-af775493eac5', 'global', NULL, 'Adductor Groin Stretch', 'adductor groin stretch', 'free_exercise_db', 'A mobility exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the adductors.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lie on your back with your feet raised towards the ceiling.
2. Have your partner hold your feet or ankles. Abduct your legs as far as you can. This will be your starting position.
3. Attempt to squeeze your legs together for 10 or more seconds, while your partner prevents you from doing so.
4. Now, relax the muscles in your legs as your partner pushes your feet apart, stretching as far as is comfortable for you. Be sure to let your partner know when the stretch is adequate to prevent overstretching or injury.', '["adductors"]', '[]', '["bodyweight"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'adductor-groin', 'mobility', 'mobility', 'time_hold', 'mobility', 'isolation', 'static', 'bilateral', 'Mild tension is fine; sharp pain is not.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Adductor_Groin', 'Adductor/Groin', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Adductor+Groin+Stretch+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Adductor_Groin.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '95171473-ba6a-5e73-ac0d-af775493eac5'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('595d506b-800b-55eb-8922-4e65cc3b14a9', 'global', NULL, 'Air Bike', 'air bike', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the abs.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lie flat on the floor with your lower back pressed to the ground. Be careful however to not strain with the neck as you perform it. Now lift your shoulders into the crunch position.
2. Bring knees up to where they are perpendicular to the floor, with your lower legs parallel to the floor. This will be your starting position.
3. Now simultaneously, slowly go through a cycle pedal motion kicking forward with the right leg and bringing in the knee of the left leg. Bring your right elbow close to your left knee by crunching to the side, as you breathe out.
4. Go back to the initial position as you breathe in.
5. Crunch to the opposite side as you cycle your legs and bring closer your left elbow to your right knee and exhale.
6. Continue alternating in this manner until all of the recommended repetitions for each side have been completed.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["stationary_bike"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'air-bike', 'strength', 'core_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'home', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Skip or modify if it aggravates lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Air_Bike', 'Air Bike', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Air+Bike+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Air_Bike.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","home_equipment_mismatch","media_new_everkinetic_match","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '595d506b-800b-55eb-8922-4e65cc3b14a9'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('cb86ad9b-b42e-57a5-8331-cdfa2dd2a98f', 'global', NULL, 'Alternate Hammer Curl', 'alternate hammer curl', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the biceps, with the forearms assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Stand up with your torso upright and a dumbbell in each hand being held at arms length. The elbows should be close to the torso.
2. The palms of the hands should be facing your torso. This will be your starting position.
3. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the right weight forward while contracting the biceps as you breathe out. Continue the movement until your biceps is fully contracted and the dumbbells are at shoulder level. Hold the contracted position for a second as you squeeze the biceps.
4. Slowly begin to bring the dumbbells back to starting position as your breathe in.
5. Repeat the movement with the left hand. This equals one repetition.
6. Continue alternating in this manner for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["biceps"]', '["forearms"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'alternate-hammer-curl', 'strength', 'elbow_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'isolation', 'pull', 'alternating', 'Use a load you can control for the whole set.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Alternate_Hammer_Curl', 'Alternate Hammer Curl', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Alternate+Hammer+Curl+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Alternate_Hammer_Curl.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'cb86ad9b-b42e-57a5-8331-cdfa2dd2a98f'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('628f1ac9-0ebf-5a43-b784-145326bc7ef1', 'global', NULL, 'Alternate Heel Touchers', 'alternate heel touchers', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the abs.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lie on the floor with the knees bent and the feet on the floor around 18-24 inches apart. Your arms should be extended by your side. This will be your starting position.
2. Crunch over your torso forward and up about 3-4 inches to the right side and touch your right heel as you hold the contraction for a second. Exhale while performing this movement.
3. Now go back slowly to the starting position as you inhale.
4. Now crunch over your torso forward and up around 3-4 inches to the left side and touch your left heel as you hold the contraction for a second. Exhale while performing this movement and then go back to the starting position as you inhale. Now that both heels have been touched, that is considered 1 repetition.
5. Continue alternating sides in this manner until all prescribed repetitions are done.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'alternate-heel-touchers', 'strength', 'core_rotation', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'isolation', 'pull', 'alternating', 'Avoid end-range twisting if it causes back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Alternate_Heel_Touchers', 'Alternate Heel Touchers', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Alternate+Heel+Touchers+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Alternate_Heel_Touchers.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '628f1ac9-0ebf-5a43-b784-145326bc7ef1'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
