2. Pull the end of the band down, and place one bent knee into the loop, ensuring it won''t slip out. Take a medium to wide grip on the bar. This will be your starting position.
3. Pull yourself upward by contracting the lats as you flex the elbow. The elbow should be driven to your side. Pull to the front, attempting to get your chin over the bar. Avoid swinging or jerking movements.
4. After a brief pause, return to the starting position.', '["lats"]', '["abs","forearms","upper_back"]', '["pull_up_bar"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'band-assisted-pull-up', 'strength', 'vertical_pull', 'reps_bodyweight', 'gym', 'compound', NULL, 'bilateral', 'Use assistance (band/machine) until you can do clean reps.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Band_Assisted_Pull-Up', 'Band Assisted Pull-Up', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Band+Assisted+Pull-up+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Band_Assisted_Pull-Up.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","media_variant_drawing","no_alternative","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '026da59b-63e6-561f-bb1b-38da5804ba42'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('20ef3756-a490-523e-b237-eafabad468fd', 'global', NULL, 'Band Back Fly', 'band back fly', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a resistance band that mainly works the front delts, with the upper back and triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Run a band around a stationary post like that of a squat rack.
2. Grab the band by the handles and stand back so that the tension in the band rises.
3. Extend and lift the arms straight in front of you. Your feet should be firmly planted on the floor spread at shoulder width. This will be your starting position.
4. As you exhale, move your arms to the sides and back. Keep your arms extended and parallel to the floor. Continue the movement until the arms are extended to your sides.
5. After a pause, go back to the original position as you inhale.
6. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["front_delts"]', '["upper_back","triceps"]', '["resistance_band"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'back-fly-with-bands', 'strength', 'shoulder_isolation', 'reps_weight', 'home', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use light loads; these are accessory movements.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Back_Flyes_-_With_Bands', 'Back Flyes - With Bands', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Band+Back+Fly+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Back_Flyes_-_With_Bands.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '20ef3756-a490-523e-b237-eafabad468fd'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('3c9e5cfd-7f8e-56ed-8711-2bfa8a1ca6a3', 'global', NULL, 'Band Calf Raise', 'band calf raise', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using a resistance band that mainly works the calves.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Grab an exercise band and stand on it with your toes making sure that the length of the band between the foot and the arms is the same for both sides.
2. While holding the handles of the band, raise the arms to the side of your head as if you were getting ready to perform a shoulder press. The palms should be facing forward with the elbows bent and to the sides. This movement will create tension on the band. This will be your starting position.
3. Keeping the hands by your shoulder, stand up on your toes as you exhale and contract the calves hard at the top of the movement.
4. After a one second contraction, slowly go back down to the starting position.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["calves"]', '[]', '["resistance_band"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'calf-raises-with-bands', 'strength', 'calf_raise', 'reps_weight', 'home', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Hold a support for balance.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Calf_Raises_-_With_Bands', 'Calf Raises - With Bands', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Band+Calf+Raise+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Calf_Raises_-_With_Bands.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","media_new_everkinetic_match","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '3c9e5cfd-7f8e-56ed-8711-2bfa8a1ca6a3'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('4fa587ad-a33b-50ce-9286-f0632862bcaf', 'global', NULL, 'Band Good Morning', 'band good morning', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a resistance band that mainly works the hamstrings, with the glutes and lower back assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Stand on the band and loop it behind your neck.
2. Stand with your feet hip-width apart and knees soft.
