3. Using your triceps to bring your torso up again, lift yourself back to the starting position.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["triceps"]', '["chest","front_delts"]', '["bench","dip_station"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'bench-dips', 'strength', 'elbow_extension', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Reduce range if you feel elbow pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Bench_Dips', 'Bench Dips', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bench+Dip+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Bench_Dips.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","home_equipment_mismatch"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '8667f449-7c4a-509d-8cbd-f54998b03fcd'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
