4. Push the dumbbell back over your chest along the same arc.', '["chest"]', '["lats","front_delts","triceps"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'bent-arm-dumbbell-pullover', 'strength', 'chest_fly', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Stop short of shoulder discomfort at the bottom.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Bent-Arm_Dumbbell_Pullover', 'Bent-Arm Dumbbell Pullover', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bent-Arm+Dumbbell+Pullover+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '6eb6e252-05bb-5b44-ae4c-43609c25982d'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('d7ce07ee-5605-5f42-90ef-b0c5fdb53d2e', 'global', NULL, 'Bent-Over Two-Dumbbell Row', 'bent-over two-dumbbell row', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the upper back, with the biceps and lats assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. With a dumbbell in each hand (palms facing your torso), bend your knees slightly and bring your torso forward by bending at the waist; as you bend make sure to keep your back straight until it is almost parallel to the floor. The weights should hang directly in front of you as your arms hang perpendicular to the floor and your torso. This is your starting position.
2. While keeping the torso stationary, lift the dumbbells to your side (as you breathe out), keeping the elbows close to the body (do not exert any force with the forearm other than holding the weights). On the top contracted position, squeeze the back muscles and hold for a second.
3. Slowly lower the weight again to the starting position as you inhale.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["upper_back"]', '["biceps","lats","front_delts"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'bent-over-two-dumbbell-row', 'strength', 'horizontal_pull', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Keep a neutral spine, especially in bent-over rows.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Bent_Over_Two-Dumbbell_Row', 'Bent Over Two-Dumbbell Row', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bent-Over+Two-Dumbbell+Row+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Bent_Over_Two-Dumbbell_Row.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'd7ce07ee-5605-5f42-90ef-b0c5fdb53d2e'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
