4. Pause briefly, then lower the cable handles slowly to the start.', '["side_delts"]', '["upper_back","traps"]', '["cable"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'cable-seated-lateral-raise', 'strength', 'shoulder_isolation', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use light loads; these are accessory movements.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Cable_Seated_Lateral_Raise', 'Cable Seated Lateral Raise', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Cable+Seated+Lateral+Raise+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '6e6afac8-7606-5c75-a475-787bd707f552'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('0a1d47d4-3497-5411-9953-fab1b7710c5e', 'global', NULL, 'Cable Shrug', 'cable shrug', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the traps.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Grasp a cable bar attachment that is attached to a low pulley with a shoulder width or slightly wider overhand (palms facing down) grip.
2. Stand erect close to the pulley with your arms extended in front of you holding the bar. This will be your starting position.
3. Lift the bar by elevating the shoulders as high as possible as you exhale. Hold the contraction at the top for a second. Refrain from using the biceps to help lift the bar. Only the shoulders should be moving up and down.
4. Lower the bar back to the original position.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["traps"]', '[]', '["cable"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'cable-shrugs', 'strength', 'shrug', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Keep the neck neutral.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Cable_Shrugs', 'Cable Shrugs', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Cable+Shrug+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Cable_Shrugs.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '0a1d47d4-3497-5411-9953-fab1b7710c5e'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('9ce330e8-2592-5dc8-9d3e-9af71695fef4', 'global', NULL, 'Cable Single-Arm Triceps Extension', 'cable single-arm triceps extension', 'free_exercise_db', 'A single-side isolation strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the triceps.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. With your right hand, grasp a single handle attached to the high-cable pulley using a supinated (underhand; palms facing up) grip. You should be standing directly in front of the weight stack.
2. Now pull the handle down so that your upper arm and elbow are locked in to the side of your body. Your upper arm and forearm should form an acute angle (less than 90-degrees). You can keep the other arm by the waist and you can have one leg in front of you and the other one back for better balance. This will be your starting position.
3. As you contract the triceps, move the single handle attachment down to your side until your arm is straight. Breathe out as you perform this movement. Your upper arms should remain stationary at all times.
4. Squeeze the triceps and hold for a second in this contracted position.
5. Slowly return the handle to the starting position.
6. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and then perform the same movement with the other arm.', '["triceps"]', '[]', '["cable"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'cable-one-arm-tricep-extension', 'strength', 'elbow_extension', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'unilateral', 'Reduce range if you feel elbow pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Cable_One_Arm_Tricep_Extension', 'Cable One Arm Tricep Extension', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Cable+Single-Arm+Triceps+Extension+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Cable_One_Arm_Tricep_Extension.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '9ce330e8-2592-5dc8-9d3e-9af71695fef4'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('011a2762-21e5-5d6d-9939-d548dc1d9af2', 'global', NULL, 'Calf Press on the Leg Press Machine', 'calf press on the leg press machine', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using the machine that mainly works the calves.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Using a leg press machine, sit down on the machine and place your legs on the platform directly in front of you at a medium (shoulder width) foot stance.
2. Lower the safety bars holding the weighted platform in place and press the platform all the way up until your legs are fully extended in front of you without locking your knees. (Note: In some leg press units you can leave the safety bars on for increased safety. If your leg press unit allows for this, then this is the preferred method of performing the exercise.) Your torso and the legs should make perfect 90-degree angle. Now carefully place your toes and balls of your feet on the lower portion of the platform with the heels extending off. Toes should be facing forward, outwards or inwards as described at the beginning of the chapter. This will be your starting position.
3. Press on the platform by raising your heels as you breathe out by extending your ankles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the knee is kept stationary at all times. There should be no bending at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down.
4. Go back slowly to the starting position as you breathe in by lowering your heels as you bend the ankles until calves are stretched.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["calves"]', '[]', '["machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'calf-press-on-the-leg-press-machine', 'strength', 'calf_raise', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Hold a support for balance.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Calf_Press_On_The_Leg_Press_Machine', 'Calf Press On The Leg Press Machine', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Calf+Press+on+the+Leg+Press+Machine+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Calf_Press_On_The_Leg_Press_Machine.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","long_step"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '011a2762-21e5-5d6d-9939-d548dc1d9af2'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
