3. Brace your core and drive through your feet to stand up, pulling the barbell close to your body.
4. Lower the barbell back down under control by pushing your hips back first.', '["lower_back"]', '["forearms","glutes","hamstrings","upper_back","quads","traps"]', '["barbell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'deficit-deadlift', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Deficit_Deadlift', 'Deficit Deadlift', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Deficit+Deadlift+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","long_step","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '27f03181-7bdc-52ce-a319-fd8b36bfc6a2'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('d7af6cfa-72c9-5e3a-af98-912692ef2d3f', 'global', NULL, 'Dip Machine', 'dip machine', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using the machine and parallel bars that mainly works the triceps, with the chest and front delts assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Sit securely in a dip machine, select the weight and firmly grasp the handles.
2. Now keep your elbows in at your sides in order to place emphasis on the triceps. The elbows should be bent at a 90 degree angle.
3. As you contract the triceps, extend your arms downwards as you exhale.
4. Now slowly let your arms come back up to the starting position as you inhale.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["triceps"]', '["chest","front_delts"]', '["machine","dip_station"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'dip-machine', 'strength', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Dip_Machine', 'Dip Machine', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dip+Machine+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Dip_Machine.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","media_new_everkinetic_match","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'd7af6cfa-72c9-5e3a-af98-912692ef2d3f'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('98da6598-f147-5a82-ad16-229ec533cd31', 'global', NULL, 'Donkey Calf Raise', 'donkey calf raise', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the calves.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Start by positioning your lower back and hips under the padded lever provided. The tailbone area should be the one making contact with the pad.
2. Place both of your arms on the side handles and place the balls of your feet on the calf block with the heels extending off. Align the toes forward, inward or outward, depending on the area you wish to target, and straighten the knees without locking them. This will be your starting position.
3. Raise your heels as you breathe out by extending your ankles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the knee is kept stationary at all times. There should be no bending at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down.
4. Go back slowly to the starting position as you breathe in by lowering your heels as you bend the ankles until calves are stretched.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["calves"]', '[]', '["other"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'donkey-calf-raises', 'strength', 'calf_raise', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Hold a support for balance.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Donkey_Calf_Raises', 'Donkey Calf Raises', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Donkey+Calf+Raise+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Donkey_Calf_Raises.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '98da6598-f147-5a82-ad16-229ec533cd31'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('0001b24c-fd72-5efb-a3b5-b646b8ccca1b', 'global', NULL, 'Double Leg Butt Kick', 'double leg butt kick', 'free_exercise_db', 'A plyometric exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the quads, with the abductors and adductors assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Begin standing with your knees slightly bent.
2. Quickly squat a short distance, flexing the hips and knees, and immediately extend to jump for maximum vertical height.
3. As you go up, tuck your heels by flexing the knees, attempting to touch the buttocks.
4. Finish the motion by landing with the knees only partially bent, using your legs to absorb the impact.', '["quads"]', '["abductors","adductors","calves","glutes","hamstrings"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'double-leg-butt-kick', 'plyometric', 'plyometric', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a forgiving surface; skip with knee/ankle pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Double_Leg_Butt_Kick', 'Double Leg Butt Kick', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Double+Leg+Butt+Kick+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Double_Leg_Butt_Kick.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '0001b24c-fd72-5efb-a3b5-b646b8ccca1b'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('a4ec4b6b-5a00-5338-bce6-22db27272a75', 'global', NULL, 'Drag Curl', 'drag curl', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a barbell that mainly works the biceps, with the forearms assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Grab a barbell with a supinated grip (palms facing forward) and get your elbows close to your torso and back. This will be your starting position.
2. As you exhale, curl the bar up while keeping the elbows to the back as you "Drag" the bar up by keeping it in contact with your torso. Also, do not lift your shoulders.
3. Slowly go back to the starting position as you keep the bar in contact with the torso at all times.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["biceps"]', '["forearms"]', '["barbell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'drag-curl', 'strength', 'elbow_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use a load you can control for the whole set.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Drag_Curl', 'Drag Curl', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Drag+Curl+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Drag_Curl.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'a4ec4b6b-5a00-5338-bce6-22db27272a75'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('ad4e4734-fcae-5d77-920e-1a483624bd5d', 'global', NULL, 'Dumbbell Alternate Biceps Curl', 'dumbbell alternate biceps curl', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the biceps, with the forearms assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Stand (torso upright) with a dumbbell in each hand held at arms length. The elbows should be close to the torso and the palms of your hand should be facing your thighs.
2. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the right weight as you rotate the palm of the hands until they are facing forward. At this point continue contracting the biceps as you breathe out until your biceps is fully contracted and the dumbbells are at shoulder level. Hold the contracted position for a second as you squeeze the biceps.
3. Slowly begin to bring the dumbbell back to the starting position as your breathe in.
4. Repeat the movement with the left hand. This equals one repetition.
5. Continue alternating in this manner for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["biceps"]', '["forearms"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'dumbbell-alternate-bicep-curl', 'strength', 'elbow_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'isolation', 'pull', 'alternating', 'Use a load you can control for the whole set.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Dumbbell_Alternate_Bicep_Curl', 'Dumbbell Alternate Bicep Curl', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dumbbell+Alternate+Biceps+Curl+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Dumbbell_Alternate_Bicep_Curl.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'ad4e4734-fcae-5d77-920e-1a483624bd5d'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('69b2567d-97cb-5839-8a26-17169ebefe14', 'global', NULL, 'Dumbbell Bench Press', 'dumbbell bench press', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the chest, with the front delts and triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lie down on a flat bench with a dumbbell in each hand resting on top of your thighs. The palms of your hands will be facing each other.
2. Then, using your thighs to help raise the dumbbells up, lift the dumbbells one at a time so that you can hold them in front of you at shoulder width.
3. Once at shoulder width, rotate your wrists forward so that the palms of your hands are facing away from you. The dumbbells should be just to the sides of your chest, with your upper arm and forearm creating a 90 degree angle. Be sure to maintain full control of the dumbbells at all times. This will be your starting position.
4. Then, as you breathe out, use your chest to push the dumbbells up. Lock your arms at the top of the lift and squeeze your chest, hold for a second and then begin coming down slowly.
5. Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.', '["chest"]', '["front_delts","triceps"]', '["dumbbell","bench"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'dumbbell-bench-press', 'strength', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Dumbbell_Bench_Press', 'Dumbbell Bench Press', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dumbbell+Bench+Press+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Dumbbell_Bench_Press.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '69b2567d-97cb-5839-8a26-17169ebefe14'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('ef170ac5-eb00-5cc4-8254-d3d57d5f7c73', 'global', NULL, 'Dumbbell Biceps Curl', 'dumbbell biceps curl', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the biceps, with the forearms assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Stand up straight with a dumbbell in each hand at arm''s length. Keep your elbows close to your torso and rotate the palms of your hands until they are facing forward. This will be your starting position.
2. Now, keeping the upper arms stationary, exhale and curl the weights while contracting your biceps. Continue to raise the weights until your biceps are fully contracted and the dumbbells are at shoulder level. Hold the contracted position for a brief pause as you squeeze your biceps.
3. Then, inhale and slowly begin to lower the dumbbells back to the starting position.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["biceps"]', '["forearms"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'dumbbell-bicep-curl', 'strength', 'elbow_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use a load you can control for the whole set.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Dumbbell_Bicep_Curl', 'Dumbbell Bicep Curl', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dumbbell+Biceps+Curl+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Dumbbell_Bicep_Curl.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'ef170ac5-eb00-5cc4-8254-d3d57d5f7c73'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('28cec5e7-ed8f-5327-86d9-f7553b4a93cc', 'global', NULL, 'Dumbbell Clean', 'dumbbell clean', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the hamstrings, with the calves and forearms assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Begin standing with a dumbbell in each hand with your feet shoulder width apart.
2. Lower the weights to the floor by flexing at the hips and knees, pushing your hips back until the dumbbells reach the floor. This will be your starting position.
3. To initiate the movement, violently jump upward by extending the hips, knees, and ankles to acclerate the weights upward. Maintaining a neutral grip on the dumbbells, keep the arms straight until full extension is reached.
4. After full extension, rebend the hips and knees to receive the weight in a squat position. Allow the arms to bend, guiding the dumbbells to your shoulders.
5. Upon receiving the weight in the squat position, extend the hips and knees to finish in a standing position with the weights on your shoulders.', '["hamstrings"]', '["calves","forearms","glutes","lower_back","quads","front_delts","traps"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'dumbbell-clean', 'strength', 'power', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Learn with a coach and light loads; power moves are technique-first.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Dumbbell_Clean', 'Dumbbell Clean', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dumbbell+Clean+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Dumbbell_Clean.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '28cec5e7-ed8f-5327-86d9-f7553b4a93cc'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('67960ba9-2a2d-56a2-8e8f-240cbfbbec30', 'global', NULL, 'Dumbbell Floor Press', 'dumbbell floor press', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the triceps, with the chest and front delts assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lay on the floor holding dumbbells in your hands. Your knees can be bent. Begin with the weights fully extended above you.
2. Lower the weights until your upper arm comes in contact with the floor. You can tuck your elbows to emphasize triceps size and strength, or to focus on your chest angle your arms to the side.
3. Pause at the bottom, and then bring the weight together at the top by extending through the elbows.', '["triceps"]', '["chest","front_delts"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'dumbbell-floor-press', 'strength', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Dumbbell_Floor_Press', 'Dumbbell Floor Press', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dumbbell+Floor+Press+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Dumbbell_Floor_Press.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '67960ba9-2a2d-56a2-8e8f-240cbfbbec30'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('7ac6d1ca-5ef1-568d-8253-6f44d8e5183a', 'global', NULL, 'Dumbbell Incline Row', 'dumbbell incline row', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the upper back, with the biceps and forearms assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Using a neutral grip, lean into an incline bench.
2. Take a dumbbell in each hand with a neutral grip, beginning with the arms straight. This will be your starting position.
3. Retract the shoulder blades and flex the elbows to row the dumbbells to your side.
