2. Place your hands either under your glutes with your palms down or by the sides holding on to the bench. This will be your starting position.
3. As you keep your legs extended, straight as possible with your knees slightly bent but locked raise your legs until they make a 90-degree angle with the floor. Exhale as you perform this portion of the movement and hold the contraction at the top for a second.
4. Now, as you inhale, slowly lower your legs back down to the starting position.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["bench"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'flat-bench-lying-leg-raise', 'strength', 'core_flexion', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Skip or modify if it aggravates lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Flat_Bench_Lying_Leg_Raise', 'Flat Bench Lying Leg Raise', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Flat+Bench+Lying+Leg+Raise+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Flat_Bench_Lying_Leg_Raise.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'f1cb49e2-8f2b-5184-97b1-28e7b365a23e'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
