2. Looking straight ahead at all times, squat as low as you can and pause at the bottom. As you squat down, push your knees out. You should squat between your legs, keeping an upright torso, with your head and chest up.
3. Rise back up by driving through your heels and repeat.', '["quads"]', '["calves","glutes"]', '["kettlebell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'front-squats-with-two-kettlebells', 'strength', 'squat', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use safety pins/spotter for heavy barbell work; stop if you feel knee or back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Front_Squats_With_Two_Kettlebells', 'Front Squats With Two Kettlebells', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Front+Squat+with+Two+Kettlebells+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Front_Squats_With_Two_Kettlebells.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '0e202853-3fd1-5c5e-8250-3e1988bf5437'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
