3. Raise the machine handles to shoulder height with control.
4. Pause briefly, then lower the machine handles slowly to the start.', '["hamstrings"]', '["calves","glutes"]', '["machine"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'glute-ham-raise', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Glute_Ham_Raise', 'Glute Ham Raise', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Glute+Ham+Raise+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","csv_match_medium","generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '15543365-d05e-5dde-9ed5-eaa0a7eaff03'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('03943bf1-62cf-5e5d-8b8e-89363dc95e73', 'global', NULL, 'Glute Kickback', 'glute kickback', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the glutes, with the hamstrings assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Kneel on the floor or an exercise mat and bend at the waist with your arms extended in front of you (perpendicular to the torso) in order to get into a kneeling push-up position but with the arms spaced at shoulder width. Your head should be looking forward and the bend of the knees should create a 90-degree angle between the hamstrings and the calves. This will be your starting position.
2. As you exhale, lift up your right leg until the hamstrings are in line with the back while maintaining the 90-degree angle bend. Contract the glutes throughout this movement and hold the contraction at the top for a second.
3. Go back to the initial position as you inhale and now repeat with the left leg.
4. Continue to alternate legs until all of the recommended repetitions have been performed.', '["glutes"]', '["hamstrings"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'glute-kickback', 'strength', 'hip_abduction_adduction', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Stay within a pain-free range.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Glute_Kickback', 'Glute Kickback', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Glute+Kickback+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Glute_Kickback.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '03943bf1-62cf-5e5d-8b8e-89363dc95e73'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('070b6e34-c68b-578e-b708-a393adab3946', 'global', NULL, 'Good Morning', 'good morning', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a barbell that mainly works the hamstrings, with the abs and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Begin with a bar on a rack at shoulder height. Rack the bar across the rear of your shoulders as you would a power squat, not on top of your shoulders. Keep your back tight, shoulder blades pinched together, and your knees slightly bent. Step back from the rack.
2. Begin by bending at the hips, moving them back as you bend over to near parallel. Keep your back arched and your cervical spine in proper alignment.
3. Reverse the motion by extending through the hips with your glutes and hamstrings. Continue until you have returned to the starting position.', '["hamstrings"]', '["abs","glutes","lower_back"]', '["barbell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'good-morning', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Good_Morning', 'Good Morning', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Good+Morning+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Good_Morning.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '070b6e34-c68b-578e-b708-a393adab3946'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
