2. Kick yourself up against the wall with your arms straight. Your body should be upside down with the arms and legs fully extended. Keep your whole body as straight as possible. Also, make sure that you keep facing the wall with your head, rather than looking down.
3. Slowly lower yourself to the ground as you inhale until your head almost touches the floor.
4. Push yourself back up slowly as you exhale until your elbows are nearly locked.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["front_delts"]', '["triceps"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'advanced', 'active', 'handstand-push-ups', 'strength', 'vertical_push', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Avoid if overhead pressing causes shoulder pain; use a landmine press instead.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Handstand_Push-Ups', 'Handstand Push-Ups', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Handstand+Push-up+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Handstand_Push-Ups.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","media_variant_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'dfa54e1a-888c-56d4-a105-1042ba0fee0a'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
