2. Hold your arms under the knees, not over (that would put to much pressure on your knee joints).
3. Slowly pull the knees toward your shoulders. This also stretches your buttocks muscles.', '["lower_back"]', '["glutes"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'hug-knees-to-chest', 'mobility', 'mobility', 'time_hold', 'mobility', 'compound', 'static', 'bilateral', 'Mild tension is fine; sharp pain is not.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Hug_Knees_To_Chest', 'Hug Knees To Chest', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Hug+Knees+to+Chest+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Hug_Knees_To_Chest.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '1eaf317d-2f5f-5bfb-870a-b76d6330d263'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('b0a0cb8b-619a-5d12-b89f-2ebd6c20a8e1', 'global', NULL, 'Hyperextension', 'hyperextension', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the lower back, with the glutes and hamstrings assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Set yourself in the hyperextension station with the pad just below your hips and your ankles secured.
2. Cross your arms over your chest.
3. Lower your torso by bending at the hips until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings.
4. Raise your torso until your body is in a straight line.', '["lower_back"]', '["glutes","hamstrings"]', '["other"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'hyperextensions-back-extensions', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Hyperextensions_Back_Extensions', 'Hyperextensions (Back Extensions)', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Hyperextension+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","csv_match_medium","generic_coaching","media_new_everkinetic_match","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'b0a0cb8b-619a-5d12-b89f-2ebd6c20a8e1'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('f9de6117-9040-5019-8bf1-9af847bf909b', 'global', NULL, 'Hyperextension with No Hyperextension Bench', 'hyperextension with no hyperextension bench', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the lower back, with the glutes and hamstrings assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. With someone holding down your legs, slide yourself down to the edge a flat bench until your hips hang off the end of the bench. Also, you will be in the same position as if you were on a hyperextension bench but the range of motion will be shorter due to the height of the flat bench vs. that of the hyperextension bench.
2. With your body straight, cross your arms in front of you (my preference) or behind your head. This will be your starting position.
3. Start bending forward slowly at the waist as far as you can while keeping your back flat. Inhale as you perform this movement. Keep moving forward until you almost touch the floor or you feel a nice stretch on the hamstrings (whichever comes first).
4. Slowly raise your torso back to the initial position as you exhale. Also, do not swing the torso at any time in order to protect the back from injury.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["lower_back"]', '["glutes","hamstrings"]', '["bench"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'hyperextensions-with-no-hyperextension-bench', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Hyperextensions_With_No_Hyperextension_Bench', 'Hyperextensions With No Hyperextension Bench', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Hyperextension+with+No+Hyperextension+Bench+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Hyperextensions_With_No_Hyperextension_Bench.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'f9de6117-9040-5019-8bf1-9af847bf909b'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('af8dd64f-225f-5b26-a878-4cdd6f0bd51e', 'global', NULL, 'Iliotibial Tract-SMR', 'iliotibial tract-smr', 'free_exercise_db', 'A mobility exercise using a foam roller that mainly works the abductors.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lay on your side, with the bottom leg placed onto a foam roller between the hip and the knee. The other leg can be crossed in front of you.
2. Place as much of your weight as is tolerable onto your bottom leg; there is no need to keep your bottom leg in contact with the ground. Be sure to relax the muscles of the leg you are stretching.
3. Roll your leg over the foam from you hip to your knee, pausing for 10-30 seconds at points of tension. Repeat with the opposite leg.', '["abductors"]', '[]', '["foam_roller"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'iliotibial-tract-foam-roll', 'mobility', 'mobility', 'time_hold', 'mobility', 'isolation', 'static', 'bilateral', 'Mild tension is fine; sharp pain is not.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Iliotibial_Tract-SMR', 'Iliotibial Tract-SMR', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Iliotibial+Tract-SMR+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Iliotibial_Tract-SMR.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'af8dd64f-225f-5b26-a878-4cdd6f0bd51e'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('0212971f-39ea-5755-a7e3-53c91b7d076e', 'global', NULL, 'Inchworm', 'inchworm', 'free_exercise_db', 'A mobility exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the hamstrings.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Stand with your feet close together. Keeping your legs straight, stretch down and put your hands on the floor directly in front of you. This will be your starting position.
2. Begin by walking your hands forward slowly, alternating your left and your right. As you do so, bend only at the hip, keeping your legs straight.
3. Keep going until your body is parallel to the ground in a pushup position.
4. Now, keep your hands in place and slowly take short steps with your feet, moving only a few inches at a time.
5. Continue walking until your feet are by hour hands, keeping your legs straight as you do so.', '["hamstrings"]', '[]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'inchworm', 'mobility', 'core_anti_extension', 'time_hold', 'home', 'compound', NULL, 'bilateral', 'Stop when form breaks rather than chasing time.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Inchworm', 'Inchworm', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Inchworm+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Inchworm.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image","no_relations"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '0212971f-39ea-5755-a7e3-53c91b7d076e'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('6214ce32-c8f7-5fce-9d9c-71d5383d49eb', 'global', NULL, 'Incline Cable Flye', 'incline cable flye', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the chest, with the front delts assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Set a bench to an incline of about 30-45 degrees and sit back against it with your feet planted, centred between two pulleys set at chest height.
2. Hold the cable handles with your arms out wide and elbows slightly bent.
3. Bring your hands together in a wide arc forward in front of your chest, squeezing your chest.
4. Return slowly along the same arc until you feel a stretch across your chest.', '["chest"]', '["front_delts"]', '["cable","bench"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'incline-cable-flye', 'strength', 'chest_fly', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Stop short of shoulder discomfort at the bottom.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Incline_Cable_Flye', 'Incline Cable Flye', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Incline+Cable+Flye+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '6214ce32-c8f7-5fce-9d9c-71d5383d49eb'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('8c19a934-f679-517d-aa37-2bf589965d2f', 'global', NULL, 'Incline Dumbbell Curl', 'incline dumbbell curl', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the biceps.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Sit back on an incline bench with a dumbbell in each hand held at arms length. Keep your elbows close to your torso and rotate the palms of your hands until they are facing forward. This will be your starting position.
2. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the weights forward while contracting the biceps as you breathe out. Only the forearms should move. Continue the movement until your biceps are fully contracted and the dumbbells are at shoulder level. Hold the contracted position for a second.
3. Slowly begin to bring the dumbbells back to starting position as your breathe in.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["biceps"]', '[]', '["dumbbell","bench"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'incline-dumbbell-curl', 'strength', 'elbow_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use a load you can control for the whole set.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Incline_Dumbbell_Curl', 'Incline Dumbbell Curl', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Incline+Dumbbell+Curl+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Curl.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","media_new_everkinetic_match","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '8c19a934-f679-517d-aa37-2bf589965d2f'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('c6c653da-eb56-5a00-b17a-77765b19bbc3', 'global', NULL, 'Incline Dumbbell Fly', 'incline dumbbell fly', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the chest, with the front delts assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Hold a dumbbell on each hand and lie on an incline bench that is set to an incline angle of no more than 30 degrees.
2. Extend your arms above you with a slight bend at the elbows.
3. Now rotate the wrists so that the palms of your hands are facing you. This will be your starting position.
4. As you breathe in, start to slowly lower the arms to the side while keeping the arms extended and while rotating the wrists until the palms of the hand are facing each other.
5. As you exhale start to bring the dumbbells back up to the starting position by reversing the motion and rotating the hands so that the pinky fingers are next to each other again. There is no motion that happens at the elbow joint.
6. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["chest"]', '["front_delts"]', '["dumbbell","bench"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'incline-dumbbell-fly', 'strength', 'chest_fly', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Stop short of shoulder discomfort at the bottom.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Incline_Dumbbell_Flyes', 'Incline Dumbbell Flyes', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Incline+Dumbbell+Fly+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Flyes.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_alternative"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'c6c653da-eb56-5a00-b17a-77765b19bbc3'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('971aa71f-9f87-53f1-912d-6dfbf3576d79', 'global', NULL, 'Incline Push-up', 'incline push-up', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the chest, with the front delts and triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Place your hands on a sturdy raised surface just wider than your shoulders and step your feet back until your body is straight.
2. Brace your core and bend your elbows to lower your chest toward the floor, keeping your elbows at about 45 degrees to your body.
3. Push the floor away to straighten your arms, keeping your hips in line with your shoulders.', '["chest"]', '["front_delts","triceps"]', '["bench"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'incline-push-up', 'strength', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Incline_Push-Up', 'Incline Push-Up', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Incline+Push-up+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","media_variant_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '971aa71f-9f87-53f1-912d-6dfbf3576d79'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('fafd2277-644a-5b02-8c62-07e4e35f3d18', 'global', NULL, 'Inverted Row', 'inverted row', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the upper back, with the lats assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Hold a bar set at waist height and walk your feet forward until your body is straight and your arms are extended.
2. Pull your chest up toward your hands, driving your elbows back.
3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the top.
4. Lower yourself slowly until your arms are straight.', '["upper_back"]', '["lats"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'inverted-row', 'strength', 'horizontal_pull', 'reps_bodyweight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Keep a neutral spine, especially in bent-over rows.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Inverted_Row', 'Inverted Row', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Inverted+Row+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'fafd2277-644a-5b02-8c62-07e4e35f3d18'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('04a96b3d-6263-501c-82a6-c91afbe63d9c', 'global', NULL, 'Jackknife Sit-up', 'jackknife sit-up', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the abs.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lie flat on the floor (or exercise mat) on your back with your arms extended straight back behind your head and your legs extended also. This will be your starting position.
2. As you exhale, bend at the waist while simultaneously raising your legs and arms to meet in a jackknife position. The upper torso should be off the floor.
3. While inhaling, lower your arms and legs back to the starting position.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'jackknife-sit-up', 'strength', 'core_flexion', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Skip or modify if it aggravates lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Jackknife_Sit-Up', 'Jackknife Sit-Up', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Jackknife+Sit-up+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Jackknife_Sit-Up.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '04a96b3d-6263-501c-82a6-c91afbe63d9c'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e0bf6eea-c8d9-57bb-a5a9-51dda9ee6673', 'global', NULL, 'JM Press', 'jm press', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a barbell that mainly works the triceps, with the chest and front delts assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Start the exercise the same way you would a close grip bench press. You will lie on a flat bench while holding a barbell at arms length (fully extended) with the elbows in. However, instead of having the arms perpendicular to the torso, make sure the bar is set in a direct line above the upper chest. This will be your starting position.
2. Now beginning from a fully extended position lower the bar down as if performing a lying triceps extension. Inhale as you perform this movement. When you reach the half way point, let the bar roll back about one inch by moving the upper arms towards your legs until they are perpendicular to the torso.
3. As you exhale, press the bar back up by using the triceps to perform a close grip bench press.
4. Now go back to the starting position and start over.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["triceps"]', '["chest","front_delts"]', '["barbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'jm-press', 'strength', 'elbow_extension', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Reduce range if you feel elbow pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'JM_Press', 'JM Press', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=JM+Press+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/JM_Press.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e0bf6eea-c8d9-57bb-a5a9-51dda9ee6673'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
