2. Bend your hips and knees to reach the weight with a flat back.
3. Brace your core and drive through your feet to stand up, pulling the kettlebell close to your body.
4. Lower the kettlebell back down under control by pushing your hips back first.
5. Finish all reps on one side, then switch sides and repeat.', '["hamstrings"]', '["glutes","lower_back"]', '["kettlebell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'kettlebell-one-legged-deadlift', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'pull', 'unilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Kettlebell_One-Legged_Deadlift', 'Kettlebell One-Legged Deadlift', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Kettlebell+One-Legged+Deadlift+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'bbc57390-bb5e-5981-8eff-65813ad6c5cc'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('167566e6-9db7-5e52-bd6b-21aee4b694f9', 'global', NULL, 'Kettlebell Pistol Squat', 'kettlebell pistol squat', 'free_exercise_db', 'A single-side compound strength exercise using a kettlebell that mainly works the quads, with the calves and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Pick up a kettlebell with two hands and hold it by the horns. Hold one leg off of the floor and squat down on the other.
2. Squat down by flexing the knee and sitting back with the hips, holding the kettlebell up in front of you.
3. Hold the bottom position for a second and then reverse the motion, driving through the heel and keeping your head and chest up.
4. Lower yourself again and repeat.
5. Finish all reps on one side, then switch sides and repeat.', '["quads"]', '["calves","glutes","hamstrings","front_delts"]', '["kettlebell"]', 'advanced', 'active', 'kettlebell-pistol-squat', 'strength', 'squat', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'unilateral', 'Use safety pins/spotter for heavy barbell work; stop if you feel knee or back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Kettlebell_Pistol_Squat', 'Kettlebell Pistol Squat', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Kettlebell+Pistol+Squat+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Kettlebell_Pistol_Squat.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '167566e6-9db7-5e52-bd6b-21aee4b694f9'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('92c2a479-9753-5464-81ba-a93ba03d239a', 'global', NULL, 'Kettlebell Sumo High Pull', 'kettlebell sumo high pull', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a kettlebell that mainly works the traps, with the adductors and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Place a kettlebell on the ground between your feet.
2. Position your feet in a wide stance, and grasp the kettlebell with two hands.
3. Set your hips back as far as possible, with your knees bent. Keep your chest and head up.
4. This will be your starting position.
5. Begin by extending the hips and knees, simultaneously pulling the kettlebell to your shoulders, raising your elbows as you do so.
6. Reverse the motion to return to the starting position.', '["traps"]', '["adductors","glutes","hamstrings","quads","front_delts"]', '["kettlebell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'kettlebell-sumo-high-pull', 'strength', 'power', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Learn with a coach and light loads; power moves are technique-first.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Kettlebell_Sumo_High_Pull', 'Kettlebell Sumo High Pull', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Kettlebell+Sumo+High+Pull+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Kettlebell_Sumo_High_Pull.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["few_steps","generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image","no_relations"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '92c2a479-9753-5464-81ba-a93ba03d239a'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('c7b0d125-bae1-5159-b435-9c6ea1070133', 'global', NULL, 'Kettlebell Thruster', 'kettlebell thruster', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a kettlebell that mainly works the front delts, with the quads and triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Clean two kettlebells to your shoulders. Clean the kettlebells to your shoulders by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebells towards your shoulders. Rotate your wrists as you do so. This will be your starting position.
2. Begin to squat by flexing your hips and knees, lowering your hips between your legs. Maintain an upright, straight back as you descend as low as you can.
3. At the bottom, reverse direction and squat by extending your knees and hips, driving through your heels. As you do so, press both kettlebells overhead by extending your arms straight up, using the momentum from the squat to help drive the weights upward.
4. As you begin the next repetition, return the weights to the shoulders.', '["front_delts"]', '["quads","triceps"]', '["kettlebell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'kettlebell-thruster', 'strength', 'power', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Learn with a coach and light loads; power moves are technique-first.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Kettlebell_Thruster', 'Kettlebell Thruster', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Kettlebell+Thruster+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Kettlebell_Thruster.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'c7b0d125-bae1-5159-b435-9c6ea1070133'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('1fc3b24f-448d-5e3e-b354-13c7163f3ab0', 'global', NULL, 'Kettlebell Turkish Get-up (Squat Style)', 'kettlebell turkish get-up (squat style)', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a kettlebell that mainly works the front delts, with the abs and calves assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lie on your back on the floor and press a kettlebell to the top position by extending the elbow. Bend the knee on the same side as the kettlebell.
2. Keeping the kettlebell locked out at all times, pivot to the opposite side and use your non- working arm to assist you in driving forward to the lunge position.
3. Using your free hand, push yourself to a seated position, then progressing to your feet. While looking up at the kettlebell, slowly stand up. Reverse the motion back to the starting position and repeat.', '["front_delts"]', '["abs","calves","hamstrings","quads","triceps"]', '["kettlebell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'kettlebell-turkish-get-up-squat-style', 'strength', 'power', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Learn with a coach and light loads; power moves are technique-first.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Kettlebell_Turkish_Get-Up_Squat_style', 'Kettlebell Turkish Get-Up (Squat style)', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Kettlebell+Turkish+Get-up+%28Squat+Style%29+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Kettlebell_Turkish_Get-Up_Squat_style.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '1fc3b24f-448d-5e3e-b354-13c7163f3ab0'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('ee99717d-b4e4-5f56-95ff-9eab3b2306f9', 'global', NULL, 'Kettlebell Windmill', 'kettlebell windmill', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a kettlebell that mainly works the abs, with the glutes and hamstrings assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Place a kettlebell in front of your lead foot and clean and press it overhead with your opposite arm. Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebell towards your shoulders. Rotate your wrist as you do so, so that the palm faces forward. Press it overhead by extending the elbow.
2. Keeping the kettlebell locked out at all times, push your butt out in the direction of the locked out kettlebell. Turn your feet out at a forty-five degree angle from the arm with the locked out kettlebell. Bending at the hip to one side, sticking your butt out, slowly lean until you can touch the floor with your free hand. Keep your eyes on the kettlebell that you hold over your head at all times.
3. Pause for a second after reaching the ground and reverse the motion back to the starting position.', '["abs"]', '["glutes","hamstrings","front_delts","triceps"]', '["kettlebell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'kettlebell-windmill', 'strength', 'core_rotation', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Avoid end-range twisting if it causes back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Kettlebell_Windmill', 'Kettlebell Windmill', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Kettlebell+Windmill+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Kettlebell_Windmill.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","long_step","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'ee99717d-b4e4-5f56-95ff-9eab3b2306f9'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('34c00fe0-5906-5e03-a909-34f1a85423b8', 'global', NULL, 'Knee Tuck Jump', 'knee tuck jump', 'free_exercise_db', 'A plyometric exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the hamstrings, with the abductors and adductors assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Begin in a comfortable standing position with your knees slightly bent. Hold your hands in front of you, palms down with your fingertips together at chest height. This will be your starting position.
2. Rapidly dip down into a quarter squat and immediately explode upward. Drive the knees towards the chest, attempting to touch them to the palms of the hands.
3. Jump as high as you can, raising your knees up, and then ensure a good land be re-extending your legs, absorbing impact through be allowing the knees to rebend.', '["hamstrings"]', '["abductors","adductors","calves","glutes","quads"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'knee-tuck-jump', 'plyometric', 'plyometric', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a forgiving surface; skip with knee/ankle pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Knee_Tuck_Jump', 'Knee Tuck Jump', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Knee+Tuck+Jump+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Knee_Tuck_Jump.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image","no_relations"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '34c00fe0-5906-5e03-a909-34f1a85423b8'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('f3a751cd-f93c-5aa9-8314-fac72078d45b', 'global', NULL, 'Knee/Hip Raise on Parallel Bars', 'knee/hip raise on parallel bars', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the abs.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Support yourself on the parallel bars with straight arms.
2. Brace your core and stop any swinging.
3. Raise your knees toward your chest.
4. Lower your legs slowly without swinging.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["other"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'knee-hip-raise-on-parallel-bars', 'strength', 'core_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Skip or modify if it aggravates lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Knee_Hip_Raise_On_Parallel_Bars', 'Knee/Hip Raise On Parallel Bars', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Knee%2FHip+Raise+on+Parallel+Bars+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'f3a751cd-f93c-5aa9-8314-fac72078d45b'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
