2. Raise the bar from the floor, taking it to shoulder height with both hands with your arms extended in front of you. Adopt a wide stance. This will be your starting position.
3. Perform the movement by rotating the trunk and hips as you swing the weight all the way down to one side. Keep your arms extended throughout the exercise.
4. Reverse the motion to swing the weight all the way to the opposite side.
5. Continue alternating the movement until the set is complete.', '["abs"]', '["glutes","lower_back","front_delts"]', '["barbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'landmine-180-s', 'strength', 'core_rotation', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Avoid end-range twisting if it causes back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Landmine_180s', 'Landmine 180''s', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Landmine+180s+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Landmine_180s.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '3752c8fb-dd6c-541c-8180-96712baa596e'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('64ef3d80-f4b3-5ea2-bc2c-fe1f203fdada', 'global', NULL, 'Lateral Bound', 'lateral bound', 'free_exercise_db', 'A plyometric exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the adductors, with the abductors and calves assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Assume a half squat position facing 90 degrees from your direction of travel. This will be your starting position.
2. Allow your lead leg to do a countermovement inward as you shift your weight to the outside leg.
3. Immediately push off and extend, attempting to bound to the side as far as possible.
4. Upon landing, immediately push off in the opposite direction, returning to your original start position.
5. Continue back and forth for several repetitions.', '["adductors"]', '["abductors","calves","glutes","hamstrings","quads"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'lateral-bound', 'plyometric', 'plyometric', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a forgiving surface; skip with knee/ankle pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Lateral_Bound', 'Lateral Bound', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Lateral+Bound+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Lateral_Bound.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image","no_relations"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '64ef3d80-f4b3-5ea2-bc2c-fe1f203fdada'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
