2. Maintaining a neutral grip, palms facing each other, begin with your arms extended directly above you, perpendicular to the floor. This will be your starting position.
3. Begin the movement by flexing the elbow, lowering the upper arms to the side. Descend until the dumbbells are to your torso.
4. Pause, then extend the elbow and return to the starting position.', '["chest"]', '["front_delts","triceps"]', '["dumbbell","bench"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'dumbbell-bench-press-with-neutral-grip', 'strength', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Dumbbell_Bench_Press_with_Neutral_Grip', 'Dumbbell Bench Press with Neutral Grip', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Neutral-Grip+Dumbbell+Bench+Press+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Dumbbell_Bench_Press_with_Neutral_Grip.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","media_variant_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '51b19b04-8533-505a-bd4a-adcde93eb7b8'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('0e1905c7-262e-51dd-a8e8-d55dbb23df03', 'global', NULL, 'One-Legged Cable Kickback', 'one-legged cable kickback', 'free_exercise_db', 'A single-side isolation strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the glutes, with the hamstrings assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Hook a leather ankle cuff to a low cable pulley and then attach the cuff to your ankle.
2. Face the weight stack from a distance of about two feet, grasping the steel frame for support.
3. While keeping your knees and hips bent slightly and your abs tight, contract your glutes to slowly "kick" the working leg back in a semicircular arc as high as it will comfortably go as you breathe out.
4. Now slowly bring your working leg forward, resisting the pull of the cable until you reach the starting position.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.
6. Switch legs and repeat the movement for the other side.', '["glutes"]', '["hamstrings"]', '["cable"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'one-legged-cable-kickback', 'strength', 'hip_abduction_adduction', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'unilateral', 'Stay within a pain-free range.', 'free_exercise_db', 'One-Legged_Cable_Kickback', 'One-Legged Cable Kickback', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=One-Legged+Cable+Kickback+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/One-Legged_Cable_Kickback.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '0e1905c7-262e-51dd-a8e8-d55dbb23df03'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('fb7d73a1-182f-5d09-8be6-4ab4fd892560', 'global', NULL, 'Overhead Lat', 'overhead lat', 'free_exercise_db', 'A mobility exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the lats, with the triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Sit upright on the floor with your partner behind you. Raise one arm straight up, and flex the elbow, attempting to touch your hand to your back. Your parner should hold your tricep and wrist. This will be your starting position.
2. Attempt to pull your upper arm to your side as your partner prevents you from doing actually doing so.
3. After 10-20 seconds, relax the arm and allow your partner to further stretch the lat by applying gentle pressure to the tricep. Hold for 10-20 seconds, and then switch sides.', '["lats"]', '["triceps"]', '["other"]', 'advanced', 'active', 'overhead-lat-stretch', 'mobility', 'mobility', 'time_hold', 'mobility', 'compound', 'static', 'bilateral', 'Mild tension is fine; sharp pain is not.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Overhead_Lat', 'Overhead Lat', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Overhead+Lat+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Overhead_Lat.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image","no_relations"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'fb7d73a1-182f-5d09-8be6-4ab4fd892560'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('7cf8b405-f395-5be8-88f6-fb14fc1ff089', 'global', NULL, 'Overhead Slam', 'overhead slam', 'free_exercise_db', 'A plyometric exercise using a medicine ball that mainly works the lats.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Hold a medine ball with both hands and stand with your feet at shoulder width. This will be your starting position.
2. Initiate the countermovement by raising the ball above your head and fully extending your body.
3. Reverse the motion, slamming the ball into the ground directly in front of you as hard as you can.
4. Receive the ball with both hands on the bounce and repeat the movement.', '["lats"]', '[]', '["medicine_ball"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'overhead-slam', 'plyometric', 'power', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Learn with a coach and light loads; power moves are technique-first.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Overhead_Slam', 'Overhead Slam', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Overhead+Slam+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Overhead_Slam.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image","no_relations"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '7cf8b405-f395-5be8-88f6-fb14fc1ff089'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('0e625ce1-2fc8-50ad-83ef-a26e7402fb1d', 'global', NULL, 'Overhead Squat', 'overhead squat', 'free_exercise_db', 'A power exercise using a barbell that mainly works the quads, with the abs and calves assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Start out by having a barbell in front of you on the floor. Your feet should be wider than shoulder width apart from each other.
2. Bend the knees and use a pronated grip (palms facing you) to grab the barbell. Your hands should be at a wider than shoulder width apart from each other before lifting. Once you are positioned, lift the barbell up until you can rest it on your chest.
3. Move the barbell over and slightly behind your head and make sure your arms are fully extended. Keep your head up at all times and also maintain a straight back. Retract your shoulder blades. This is your starting position.
4. Slowly lower the weight by bending your knees until your thighs are parallel to the ground while inhaling.
5. Now use your feet and legs to help bring the weight back up to the starting position while exhaling.
6. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["quads"]', '["abs","calves","glutes","hamstrings","lower_back","front_delts","triceps"]', '["barbell"]', 'advanced', 'active', 'overhead-squat', 'power', 'squat', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use safety pins/spotter for heavy barbell work; stop if you feel knee or back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Overhead_Squat', 'Overhead Squat', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Overhead+Squat+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Overhead_Squat.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '0e625ce1-2fc8-50ad-83ef-a26e7402fb1d'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('c3add3b5-045a-522e-ab33-33c19cf0c555', 'global', NULL, 'Pallof Press', 'pallof press', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the abs, with the chest and front delts assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Connect a standard handle to a tower, and—if possible—position the cable to shoulder height. If not, a low pulley will suffice.
2. With your side to the cable, grab the handle with both hands and step away from the tower. You should be approximately arm''s length away from the pulley, with the tension of the weight on the cable.
3. With your feet positioned hip-width apart and knees slightly bent, hold the cable to the middle of your chest. This will be your starting position.
4. Press the cable away from your chest, fully extending both arms. You core should be tight and engaged.
5. Hold the repetition for several seconds before returning to the starting position.
6. At the conclusion of the set, repeat facing the other direction.', '["abs"]', '["chest","front_delts","triceps"]', '["cable"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'pallof-press', 'strength', 'core_rotation', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Avoid end-range twisting if it causes back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Pallof_Press', 'Pallof Press', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Pallof+Press+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Pallof_Press.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'c3add3b5-045a-522e-ab33-33c19cf0c555'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
