2. Use your fingers to grip the outside part of the plate and your thumb for the other side thus holding both plates together. This is the starting position.
3. Squeeze the plate with your fingers and thumb. Hold this position for as long as you can.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of sets prescribed in your program.
5. Switch arms and repeat the movements.', '["forearms"]', '[]', '["other"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'plate-pinch', 'strength', 'forearm_grip', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'static', 'bilateral', 'Stop if you feel wrist pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Plate_Pinch', 'Plate Pinch', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Plate+Pinch+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Plate_Pinch.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'd8a555e3-a2ea-57ea-93db-ebf1e1973d5f'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('cc934012-55ea-5984-9aa9-6ff3ec427ea7', 'global', NULL, 'Plie Dumbbell Squat', 'plie dumbbell squat', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the quads, with the abs and calves assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Hold a dumbbell at the base with both hands and stand straight up. Move your legs so that they are wider than shoulder width apart from each other with your knees slightly bent.
2. Your toes should be facing out. This is the starting position.
3. Slowly bend the knees and lower your legs until your thighs are parallel to the floor. Make sure to inhale as this is the eccentric part of the exercise.
4. Press mainly with the heel of the foot to bring the body back to the starting position while exhaling.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["quads"]', '["abs","calves","glutes","hamstrings"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'plie-dumbbell-squat', 'strength', 'squat', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use safety pins/spotter for heavy barbell work; stop if you feel knee or back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Plie_Dumbbell_Squat', 'Plie Dumbbell Squat', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Plie+Dumbbell+Squat+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Plie_Dumbbell_Squat.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'cc934012-55ea-5984-9aa9-6ff3ec427ea7'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('ee6da9da-d08c-577d-a025-0799c1a05bbc', 'global', NULL, 'Plyo Push-up', 'plyo push-up', 'free_exercise_db', 'A plyometric exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the chest, with the front delts and triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Move into a prone position on the floor, supporting your weight on your hands and toes.
2. Your arms should be fully extended with the hands around shoulder width. Keep your body straight throughout the movement. This will be your starting position.
3. Descend by flexing at the elbow, lowering your chest towards the ground.
4. At the bottom, reverse the motion by pushing yourself up through elbow extension as quickly as possible. Attempt to push your upper body up until your hands leave the ground.
5. Return to the starting position and repeat the exercise.
6. For added difficulty, add claps into the movement while you are air borne.', '["chest"]', '["front_delts","triceps"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'plyo-push-up', 'plyometric', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Plyo_Push-up', 'Plyo Push-up', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Plyo+Push-up+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Plyo_Push-up.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","media_variant_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'ee6da9da-d08c-577d-a025-0799c1a05bbc'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('ee116ad3-f1d2-5eab-ace6-ad91959d039f', 'global', NULL, 'Power Clean', 'power clean', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a barbell that mainly works the hamstrings, with the calves and forearms assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Stand with your feet slightly wider than shoulder width apart and toes pointing out slightly. Squat down and grasp bar with a closed, pronated grip. Your hands should be slightly wider than shoulder width apart outside knees with elbows fully extended. Place the bar about 1 inch in front of your shins and over the balls of your feet. Your back should be flat or slightly arched, your chest held up and out and your shoulder blades should be retracted.
2. Keep your head in a neutral position (in line with vertebral column and not tilted or rotated) with your eyes focused straight ahead. Inhale during this phase. Lift the bar from the floor by forcefully extending the hips and the knees as you exhale. Do not bend at the waist yet and do not let the hips rise before the shoulders (this would have the effect of pushing the glutes in the air and stretching the hamstrings. Keep elbows fully extended with the head in a neutral position and the shoulders over the bar. As the bar raises keep it as close to the shins as possible.
3. As the bar passes the knees, thrust your hips forward and slightly bend the knees to avoid locking them. Keep the back flat or slightly arched, elbows fully extended and your head neutral. Inhale and then forcefully and quickly extend your hips and knees and stand on your toes. Keep the bar as close to your body as possible. Also, keep your shoulders over the bar and arms straight as long as possible.
4. When your lower body joints are fully extended, shrug the shoulders upward rapidly without letting the elbows flex yet. Exhale during this portion of the movement. As the shoulders reach their highest elevation flex your elbows to begin pulling your body under the bar. Continue to pull the arms as high and as long as possible. After the lower body has fully extended and the bar reaches near maximal height, pull your body under the bar and rotate the arms around and under the bar.
5. Simultaneously, flex the hips and knees into a quarter squat position. Once the arms are under the bar, inhale and then lift your elbows to position the upper arms parallel to the floor. Rack the bar across the front of your collar bones and front shoulder muscles. Catch the bar with an erect and tight torso, a neutral head position and flat feet. Exhale during this movement. Stand up by extending the hips and knees to a fully erect position.
6. Lower the bar by gradually reducing the muscular tension of the arms to allow a controlled descent of the bar to the thighs. Inhale during this movement. Simultaneously flex the hips and knees to cushion the impact of the bar on the thighs. Squat down with the elbows fully extended until the bar touches the floor. Start over at Phase 1 and repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["hamstrings"]', '["calves","forearms","glutes","lower_back","upper_back","quads","front_delts","traps","triceps"]', '["barbell"]', 'advanced', 'active', 'power-clean', 'strength', 'power', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Learn with a coach and light loads; power moves are technique-first.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Power_Clean', 'Power Clean', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Power+Clean+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Power_Clean.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'ee116ad3-f1d2-5eab-ace6-ad91959d039f'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('1658e26a-5b19-502f-bf83-7235ed184fd9', 'global', NULL, 'Power Snatch', 'power snatch', 'free_exercise_db', 'A power exercise using a barbell that mainly works the hamstrings, with the calves and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Begin with a loaded barbell on the floor. The bar should be close to or touching the shins, and a wide grip should be taken on the bar. The feet should be directly below the hips, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hips, with the chest up and the head looking forward. The shoulders should be just in front of the bar. This will be the starting position.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar from the ground. The back angle should stay the same until the bar passes the knees.
3. Transition into the second pull by extending through the hips knees and ankles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body. At peak extension, shrug the shoulders and allow the elbows to flex to the side.
4. As you move your feet into the receiving position, a slightly wider position, pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. The bar should be received in a partial squat. Continue raising the bar to the overhead position, receiving the bar locked out overhead.
5. Return to a standing position with the weight over head.', '["hamstrings"]', '["calves","glutes","lower_back","quads","front_delts","traps","triceps"]', '["barbell"]', 'advanced', 'active', 'power-snatch', 'power', 'power', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Learn with a coach and light loads; power moves are technique-first.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Power_Snatch', 'Power Snatch', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Power+Snatch+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Power_Snatch.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '1658e26a-5b19-502f-bf83-7235ed184fd9'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('200c9fb6-5f0f-5ded-9888-49f110a2b4e0', 'global', NULL, 'Preacher Curl', 'preacher curl', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using a barbell that mainly works the biceps.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. To perform this movement you will need a preacher bench and an E-Z bar. Grab the E-Z curl bar at the close inner handle (either have someone hand you the bar which is preferable or grab the bar from the front bar rest provided by most preacher benches). The palm of your hands should be facing forward and they should be slightly tilted inwards due to the shape of the bar.
2. With the upper arms positioned against the preacher bench pad and the chest against it, hold the E-Z Curl Bar at shoulder length. This will be your starting position.
3. As you breathe in, slowly lower the bar until your upper arm is extended and the biceps is fully stretched.
4. As you exhale, use the biceps to curl the weight up until your biceps is fully contracted and the bar is at shoulder height. Squeeze the biceps hard and hold this position for a second.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["biceps"]', '[]', '["barbell","bench"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'preacher-curl', 'strength', 'elbow_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use a load you can control for the whole set.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Preacher_Curl', 'Preacher Curl', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Preacher+Curl+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Preacher_Curl.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '200c9fb6-5f0f-5ded-9888-49f110a2b4e0'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('ebef52b2-dd11-5ad5-892e-68f505966591', 'global', NULL, 'Pull Through', 'pull through', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the glutes, with the hamstrings and lower back assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Stand facing away from a low pulley with the rope between your legs.
2. Hinge at your hips to reach your hands back through your legs.
3. Drive your hips forward to stand tall, pulling the load through.
4. Squeeze your glutes at the top before the next rep.', '["glutes"]', '["hamstrings","lower_back"]', '["cable"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'pull-through', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Pull_Through', 'Pull Through', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Pull+Through+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["few_steps","generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'ebef52b2-dd11-5ad5-892e-68f505966591'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('165eaec6-8da7-5acd-a276-baa3429e889e', 'global', NULL, 'Push Press', 'push press', 'free_exercise_db', 'A power exercise with a barbell that mainly works the front shoulders, with the quads and triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:fitbud_curated', '1. Stand tall with your feet about hip-width apart.
2. Hold the barbell at shoulder height.
3. Dip slightly at your knees, then drive up through your legs to press the barbell straight overhead until your arms are straight.
4. Lower the barbell under control back to shoulder height.', '["front_delts"]', '["quads","triceps"]', '["barbell"]', 'advanced', 'active', 'push-press', 'power', 'vertical_push', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Avoid if overhead pressing causes shoulder pain; use a landmine press instead.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Push_Press', 'Push Press', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Push+Press+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["ai_authored_steps","csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '165eaec6-8da7-5acd-a276-baa3429e889e'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
