2. Select the desired option from the menu.
3. You may have to start pedaling to turn it on.
4. You can use the manual setting, or you can select a program to use.
5. The level of resistance can be changed throughout the workout.
6. The handles can be used to monitor your heart rate to help you stay at an appropriate intensity.', '["quads"]', '["calves","glutes","hamstrings"]', '["machine","stationary_bike"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'recumbent-bike', 'cardio', 'locomotion', 'distance_time', 'cardio', 'compound', NULL, 'bilateral', 'Stop if you feel chest pain, dizziness or unusual breathlessness.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Recumbent_Bike', 'Recumbent Bike', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Recumbent+Bike+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Recumbent_Bike.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","long_step","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'dc1110e1-1a5b-5518-9cba-02b20b4b1485'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('f8f66b40-b70b-58ba-9819-823bed5454e8', 'global', NULL, 'Reverse Barbell Curl', 'reverse barbell curl', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using a barbell that mainly works the biceps, with the forearms assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Stand up with your torso upright while holding a barbell at shoulder width with the elbows close to the torso. The palm of your hands should be facing down (pronated grip). This will be your starting position.
2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the weights while contracting the biceps as you breathe out. Only the forearms should move. Continue the movement until your biceps are fully contracted and the bar is at shoulder level. Hold the contracted position for a second as you squeeze the muscle.
3. Slowly begin to bring the bar back to starting position as your breathe in.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["biceps"]', '["forearms"]', '["barbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'reverse-barbell-curl', 'strength', 'elbow_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use a load you can control for the whole set.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Reverse_Barbell_Curl', 'Reverse Barbell Curl', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Reverse+Barbell+Curl+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Reverse_Barbell_Curl.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","csv_match_medium","generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'f8f66b40-b70b-58ba-9819-823bed5454e8'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('06216468-d801-5000-b9ee-54fd8ca9e8cc', 'global', NULL, 'Reverse Crunch', 'reverse crunch', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the abs.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lie down on the floor with your legs fully extended and arms to the side of your torso with the palms on the floor. Your arms should be stationary for the entire exercise.
2. Move your legs up so that your thighs are perpendicular to the floor and feet are together and parallel to the floor. This is the starting position.
3. While inhaling, move your legs towards the torso as you roll your pelvis backwards and you raise your hips off the floor. At the end of this movement your knees will be touching your chest.
4. Hold the contraction for a second and move your legs back to the starting position while exhaling.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'reverse-crunch', 'strength', 'core_flexion', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Skip or modify if it aggravates lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Reverse_Crunch', 'Reverse Crunch', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Reverse+Crunch+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Reverse_Crunch.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '06216468-d801-5000-b9ee-54fd8ca9e8cc'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
