2. To begin the movement, flex the hips, pulling the legs forward.
3. Reverse the motion by extending the hips, kicking the leg back. It is very important not to over-extend the hip on this movement, stopping short of your full range of motion.
4. Return by again flexing the hip, pulling the carriage forward as far as you can.
5. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.', '["hamstrings"]', '["calves","glutes"]', '["machine"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'reverse-hyperextension', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Reverse_Hyperextension', 'Reverse Hyperextension', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Reverse+Hyperextension+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Reverse_Hyperextension.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '483007ed-4b6c-5a81-bfb2-9bbfc5bfcf00'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
