2. In a semicircular motion, pull your hands out to your side and back, contracting your rear delts.
3. Keep your arms slightly bent throughout the movement, with all of the motion occurring at the shoulder joint.
4. Pause at the rear of the movement, and slowly return the weight to the starting position.', '["front_delts"]', '[]', '["machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'reverse-machine-fly', 'strength', 'shoulder_isolation', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use light loads; these are accessory movements.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Reverse_Machine_Flyes', 'Reverse Machine Flyes', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Reverse+Machine+Fly+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Reverse_Machine_Flyes.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '600bf03d-f9b7-5500-9362-74456fe06ed4'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
