2. Turn the rope from your wrists, keeping your elbows close to your sides.
3. Jump just high enough to clear the rope with each turn.
4. Land softly on the balls of your feet and keep a steady rhythm.', '["quads"]', '["calves","hamstrings"]', '["jump_rope"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'jump-rope-skipping', 'cardio', 'locomotion', 'time', 'cardio', 'compound', NULL, 'bilateral', 'Stop if you feel chest pain, dizziness or unusual breathlessness.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Rope_Jumping', 'Rope Jumping', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Rope+Jumping+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["ai_authored_steps","csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'c8f5b42c-4f85-5a67-81a3-cbede7e032c1'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('af26be3b-6c7f-5994-9008-b11ed4e03465', 'global', NULL, 'Rope Straight-Arm Pulldown', 'rope straight-arm pulldown', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the lats.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Attach a rope to a high pulley and make your weight selection. Stand a couple feet back from the pulley with your feet staggered and take the rope with both hands. Lean forward from the hip, keeping your back straight, with your arms extended up in front of you. This will be your starting position.
2. Keeping your arms straight, extend the shoulder to pull the rope down to your thighs.
3. Pause at the bottom of the motion, squeezing your lats.
4. Return to the starting position without allowing the weight to fully rest on the stack.', '["lats"]', '[]', '["cable"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'rope-straight-arm-pulldown', 'strength', 'vertical_pull', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use assistance (band/machine) until you can do clean reps.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Rope_Straight-Arm_Pulldown', 'Rope Straight-Arm Pulldown', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Rope+Straight-Arm+Pulldown+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Rope_Straight-Arm_Pulldown.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'af26be3b-6c7f-5994-9008-b11ed4e03465'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('d2a2e034-0e9b-592c-9d3f-19a63b0ed156', 'global', NULL, 'Rope Triceps Pushdown', 'rope triceps pushdown', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the triceps.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Attach a rope attachment to a high pulley and grab with a neutral grip (palms facing each other).
2. Standing upright with the torso straight and a very small inclination forward, bring the upper arms close to your body and perpendicular to the floor. The forearms should be pointing up towards the pulley as they hold the rope with the palms facing each other. This is your starting position.
3. Using the triceps, bring the rope down as you bring each side of the rope to the side of your thighs. At the end of the movement the arms are fully extended and perpendicular to the floor. The upper arms should always remain stationary next to your torso and only the forearms should move. Exhale as you perform this movement.
4. After holding for a second, at the contracted position, bring the rope slowly up to the starting point. Breathe in as you perform this step.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["triceps"]', '[]', '["cable"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'triceps-pushdown-rope-attachment', 'strength', 'elbow_extension', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Reduce range if you feel elbow pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Triceps_Pushdown_-_Rope_Attachment', 'Triceps Pushdown - Rope Attachment', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Rope+Triceps+Pushdown+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Triceps_Pushdown_-_Rope_Attachment.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","image_match_uncertain","media_match_medium"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'd2a2e034-0e9b-592c-9d3f-19a63b0ed156'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('d771c0ff-bee8-5ef4-a7ba-943ed74c37d0', 'global', NULL, 'Rowing Machine', 'rowing machine', 'free_exercise_db', 'A cardio exercise using the machine that mainly works the quads, with the biceps and calves assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. To begin, seat yourself on the rower. Make sure that your heels are resting comfortably against the base of the foot pedals and that the straps are secured. Select the program that you wish to use, if applicable. Sit up straight and bend forward at the hips.
2. There are three phases of movement when using a rower. The first phase is when you come forward on the rower. Your knees are bent and against your chest. Your upper body is leaning slightly forward while still maintaining good posture. Next, push against the foot pedals and extend your legs while bringing your hands to your upper abdominal area, squeezing your shoulders back as you do so. To avoid straining your back, use primarily your leg and hip muscles.
3. The recovery phase simply involves straightening your arms, bending the knees, and bringing your body forward again as you transition back into the first phase.', '["quads"]', '["biceps","calves","glutes","hamstrings","lower_back","upper_back"]', '["machine","rowing_machine"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'rowing-machine', 'cardio', 'locomotion', 'distance_time', 'cardio', 'compound', NULL, 'bilateral', 'Stop if you feel chest pain, dizziness or unusual breathlessness.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Rowing_Stationary', 'Rowing, Stationary', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Rowing+Machine+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Rowing_Stationary.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","long_step","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'd771c0ff-bee8-5ef4-a7ba-943ed74c37d0'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
