2. Keep the front heel on the floor (if it lifts up, scoot your other leg further back).
3. Place your hands on either side of your front leg. To get more out of this stretch, push your butt up toward the ceiling, and then gradually lower it back toward the floor. You''ll Stretch the hip flexor of the back leg and the hamstring and buttocks of the front.', '["hamstrings"]', '["calves"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'runner-s-stretch', 'mobility', 'mobility', 'time_hold', 'mobility', 'compound', 'static', 'bilateral', 'Mild tension is fine; sharp pain is not.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Runners_Stretch', 'Runner''s Stretch', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Runner%27s+Stretch+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Runners_Stretch.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'bb4d541b-2043-5ab2-8c77-9e1f7083fc35'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
