2. Maintain good posture, and place your free hand behind your back. This will be your starting position.
3. Lower yourself by allowing the elbow to flex until you touch the ground.
4. Descend slowly, and reverse direction be extending the arm to return to the starting position.
5. Finish all reps on one side, then switch sides and repeat.', '["chest"]', '["front_delts","triceps"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'single-arm-push-up', 'strength', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', 'push', 'unilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Single-Arm_Push-Up', 'Single-Arm Push-Up', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Single-Arm+Push-up+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Single-Arm_Push-Up.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","media_variant_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '844cf92a-48f4-517f-8087-1c6c439ea6ac'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
