2. Curl your hips off the floor by pulling your knees toward your chest.
3. Pause briefly with your abs squeezed.
4. Lower your hips slowly back to the floor.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["machine","smith_machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'smith-machine-hip-raise', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Smith_Machine_Hip_Raise', 'Smith Machine Hip Raise', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Smith+Machine+Hip+Raise+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative","no_drawing","no_image","no_relations","pattern_muscle_mismatch","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '49194209-7466-5dee-8fe1-ea80d991b077'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('e9047eae-d133-52ef-adaf-441e48b9d299', 'global', NULL, 'Smith Machine Incline Bench Press', 'smith machine incline bench press', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using the machine and a Smith machine that mainly works the chest, with the front delts and triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Place an incline bench underneath the smith machine. Place the barbell at a height that you can reach when lying down and your arms are almost fully extended. Once the weight you need is selected, lie down on the incline bench and make sure your upper chest is aligned with the barbell. Using a pronated grip (palms facing forward) that is wider than shoulder width, unlock the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with your arms locked. This will be your starting position.
2. As you breathe in, come down slowly until you feel the bar on your upper chest.
3. After a second pause, bring the bar back to the starting position as you breathe out and push the bar using your chest muscles. Lock your arms in the contracted position, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly again.
4. Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
5. When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.', '["chest"]', '["front_delts","triceps"]', '["machine","bench","smith_machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'smith-machine-incline-bench-press', 'strength', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Smith_Machine_Incline_Bench_Press', 'Smith Machine Incline Bench Press', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Smith+Machine+Incline+Bench+Press+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Smith_Machine_Incline_Bench_Press.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","long_step"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'e9047eae-d133-52ef-adaf-441e48b9d299'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('c50a4b74-054a-5889-aa47-5f00aa9a72ad', 'global', NULL, 'Smith Machine Overhead Shoulder Press', 'smith machine overhead shoulder press', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using the machine and a Smith machine that mainly works the front delts, with the triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Stand tall with your feet about hip-width apart.
2. Hold the Smith machine bar at shoulder height.
3. Brace your core and press the Smith machine bar straight overhead until your arms are straight.
4. Lower the Smith machine bar under control back to shoulder height.', '["front_delts"]', '["triceps"]', '["machine","smith_machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'smith-machine-overhead-shoulder-press', 'strength', 'vertical_push', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Avoid if overhead pressing causes shoulder pain; use a landmine press instead.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Smith_Machine_Overhead_Shoulder_Press', 'Smith Machine Overhead Shoulder Press', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Smith+Machine+Overhead+Shoulder+Press+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'c50a4b74-054a-5889-aa47-5f00aa9a72ad'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('39fe47b1-cdc7-5088-b4a7-abb5c681cf1d', 'global', NULL, 'Smith Machine Squat', 'smith machine squat', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using the machine and a Smith machine that mainly works the quads, with the calves and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. To begin, first set the bar on the height that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side (palms facing forward), unlock it and lift it off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.
3. Position your legs using a shoulder width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up at all times and also maintain a straight back.
4. Begin to slowly lower the bar by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calves becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to the floor). Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. If your knees are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the starting position.
6. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["quads"]', '["calves","glutes","hamstrings","lower_back"]', '["machine","smith_machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'smith-machine-squat', 'strength', 'squat', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use safety pins/spotter for heavy barbell work; stop if you feel knee or back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Smith_Machine_Squat', 'Smith Machine Squat', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Smith+Machine+Squat+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Smith_Machine_Squat.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '39fe47b1-cdc7-5088-b4a7-abb5c681cf1d'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('835309e0-e7b4-51e2-b852-6b65b20ea3f7', 'global', NULL, 'Smith Machine Stiff-Leg Deadlift', 'smith machine stiff-leg deadlift', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using the machine and a Smith machine that mainly works the hamstrings, with the glutes and lower back assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. To begin, set the bar on the smith machine to a height that is around the middle of your thighs. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, grasp the bar using a pronated (palms forward) grip that is shoulder width apart. You may need some wrist wraps if using a significant amount of weight.
2. Lift the bar up by fully extending your arms while keeping your back straight. Stand with your torso straight and your legs spaced using a shoulder width or narrower stance. The knees should be slightly bent. This is your starting position.
3. Keeping the knees stationary, lower the barbell to over the top of your feet by bending at the waist while keeping your back straight. Keep moving forward as if you were going to pick something from the floor until you feel a stretch on the hamstrings. Exhale as you perform this movement.
4. Start bringing your torso up straight again as soon as you feel the hamstrings stretch by extending your hips and waist until you are back at the starting position. Inhale as you perform this movement.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["hamstrings"]', '["glutes","lower_back"]', '["machine","smith_machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'smith-machine-stiff-legged-deadlift', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Smith_Machine_Stiff-Legged_Deadlift', 'Smith Machine Stiff-Legged Deadlift', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Smith+Machine+Stiff-Leg+Deadlift+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Smith_Machine_Stiff-Legged_Deadlift.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '835309e0-e7b4-51e2-b852-6b65b20ea3f7'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('93aadd22-bb02-577f-8508-d351a985cb62', 'global', NULL, 'Smith Single-Leg Split Squat', 'smith single-leg split squat', 'free_exercise_db', 'A single-side compound strength exercise using the machine and a Smith machine that mainly works the quads, with the calves and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Set the Smith machine bar across your upper back, working on one leg at a time.
2. Take a long split stance with your back heel lifted.
3. Lower your back knee straight down toward the floor until your front thigh is about parallel.
4. Drive through your front foot to rise back up.
5. Finish all reps on one side, then switch legs.', '["quads"]', '["calves","glutes","hamstrings"]', '["machine","smith_machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'smith-single-leg-split-squat', 'strength', 'lunge', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'unilateral', 'Hold a support for balance if needed; keep loads light until balance is solid.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Smith_Single-Leg_Split_Squat', 'Smith Single-Leg Split Squat', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Smith+Single-Leg+Split+Squat+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '93aadd22-bb02-577f-8508-d351a985cb62'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
