2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the weights while contracting the biceps as you breathe out. Only the forearms should move. Continue the movement until your biceps are fully contracted and the bar is at shoulder level. Hold the contracted position for a second as you squeeze the muscle.
3. Slowly begin to bring the curl bar back to starting position as your breathe in.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["biceps"]', '[]', '["cable"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'standing-biceps-cable-curl', 'strength', 'elbow_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use a load you can control for the whole set.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Standing_Biceps_Cable_Curl', 'Standing Biceps Cable Curl', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Standing+Biceps+Cable+Curl+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Standing_Biceps_Cable_Curl.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'a76bd70c-5576-5730-b5be-c9e9a76d9ac0'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
