2. Hold the dumbbells in front of your thighs with an overhand grip, hands about shoulder-width apart.
3. Pull the dumbbells straight up along your body to chest height, leading with your elbows.
4. Lower the dumbbells slowly back to your thighs.', '["traps"]', '["biceps","side_delts"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'standing-dumbbell-upright-row', 'strength', 'shoulder_isolation', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use light loads; these are accessory movements.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Standing_Dumbbell_Upright_Row', 'Standing Dumbbell Upright Row', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Standing+Dumbbell+Upright+Row+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '8aef6fe6-2249-56a9-9354-a91dab862f18'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('78a085bf-70e8-57a0-8353-7a37d53520e5', 'global', NULL, 'Standing Hip Circle', 'standing hip circle', 'free_exercise_db', 'A mobility exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the abductors, with the adductors assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Begin standing on one leg, holding to a vertical support.
2. Raise the unsupported knee to 90 degrees. This will be your starting position.
3. Open the hip as far as possible, attempting to make a big circle with your knee.
4. Perform this movement slowly for a number of repetitions, and repeat on the other side.', '["abductors"]', '["adductors"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'standing-hip-circles', 'mobility', 'mobility', 'time_hold', 'mobility', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Mild tension is fine; sharp pain is not.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Standing_Hip_Circles', 'Standing Hip Circles', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Standing+Hip+Circle+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Standing_Hip_Circles.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '78a085bf-70e8-57a0-8353-7a37d53520e5'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
