2. Now communicate with your partner so that he/she can grip the other side of the towel to apply resistance. Keeping your upper arms close to your head (elbows in) and perpendicular to the floor, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind your head until your forearms touch your biceps. Breathe in as you perform this step.
3. Go back to the starting position by using the triceps to raise the towel. Breathe out as you perform this step.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["triceps"]', '[]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'standing-towel-triceps-extension', 'strength', 'elbow_extension', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Reduce range if you feel elbow pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Standing_Towel_Triceps_Extension', 'Standing Towel Triceps Extension', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Standing+Towel+Triceps+Extension+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Standing_Towel_Triceps_Extension.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '68818dbc-48c8-5a53-8fbd-02832153a3c9'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
