2. Now, while keeping your upper arms stationary, exhale and use your triceps to lift the weights until the arm is fully extended. Focus on moving the forearm.
3. After a brief pause at the top contraction, inhale and slowly lower the dumbbells back down to the starting position.
4. Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', '["triceps"]', '[]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'tricep-dumbbell-kickback', 'strength', 'elbow_extension', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Reduce range if you feel elbow pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Tricep_Dumbbell_Kickback', 'Tricep Dumbbell Kickback', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Triceps+Dumbbell+Kickback+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Tricep_Dumbbell_Kickback.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","long_step","media_new_everkinetic_match","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'c6424eeb-6b8f-5a89-8f48-1492c2b29f70'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
