2. Your legs should be crossed by wrapping one ankle around the other. Slowly elevate your legs up in the air until your thighs are perpendicular to the floor with a slight bend at the knees.
3. Move your arms from the floor and cross them so they are resting on your chest. This is the starting position.
4. While keeping your lower back pressed against the floor, slowly lift your torso. Remember to exhale while perform this part of the exercise.
5. Slowly begin to lower your torso back down to the starting position while inhaling.
6. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'tuck-crunch', 'strength', 'core_flexion', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Skip or modify if it aggravates lower-back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Tuck_Crunch', 'Tuck Crunch', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Tuck+Crunch+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Tuck_Crunch.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '89b438da-a39d-51ea-8cc7-2aa6a4bc95f6'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
