4. Release slowly and repeat if needed.', '["upper_back"]', '[]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'upper-back-stretch', 'mobility', 'mobility', 'time_hold', 'mobility', 'isolation', 'static', 'bilateral', 'Mild tension is fine; sharp pain is not.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Upper_Back_Stretch', 'Upper Back Stretch', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Upper+Back+Stretch+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["few_steps","generic_coaching","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '1e8551c1-5d88-569b-8205-a453dd59fbbd'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('f5484b3c-7da7-56e0-a681-2fee172959d8', 'global', NULL, 'Upright Barbell Row', 'upright barbell row', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a barbell that mainly works the front delts, with the traps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Grasp a barbell with an overhand grip that is slightly less than shoulder width. The bar should be resting on the top of your thighs with your arms extended and a slight bend in your elbows. Your back should also be straight. This will be your starting position.
2. Now exhale and use the sides of your shoulders to lift the bar, raising your elbows up and to the side. Keep the bar close to your body as you raise it. Continue to lift the bar until it nearly touches your chin. Remember to keep your torso stationary and pause for a second at the top of the movement.
3. Lower the bar back down slowly to the starting position. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["front_delts"]', '["traps"]', '["barbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'upright-barbell-row', 'strength', 'shoulder_isolation', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use light loads; these are accessory movements.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Upright_Barbell_Row', 'Upright Barbell Row', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Upright+Barbell+Row+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Upright_Barbell_Row.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'f5484b3c-7da7-56e0-a681-2fee172959d8'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('1d3441fc-6f01-504e-a583-b73eee60de7d', 'global', NULL, 'Upright Cable Row', 'upright cable row', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the traps, with the front delts assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Grasp a straight bar cable attachment that is attached to a low pulley with a pronated (palms facing your thighs) grip that is slightly less than shoulder width. The bar should be resting on top of your thighs. Your arms should be extended with a slight bend at the elbows and your back should be straight. This will be your starting position.
2. Use your side shoulders to lift the cable bar as you exhale. The bar should be close to the body as you move it up. Continue to lift it until it nearly touches your chin. As you lift the bar, your elbows should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torso stationary and pause for a second at the top of the movement.
3. Lower the bar back down slowly to the starting position. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["traps"]', '["front_delts"]', '["cable"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'upright-cable-row', 'strength', 'shoulder_isolation', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use light loads; these are accessory movements.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Upright_Cable_Row', 'Upright Cable Row', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Upright+Cable+Row+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Upright_Cable_Row.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '1d3441fc-6f01-504e-a583-b73eee60de7d'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('9b1a6360-22d6-5e96-9b01-cca2e1b42960', 'global', NULL, 'V-Bar Pull-up', 'v-bar pull-up', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a pull-up bar that mainly works the lats, with the biceps and upper back assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Start by placing the middle of the V-bar in the middle of the pull-up bar (assuming that the pull-up station you are using does not have neutral grip handles). The V-Bar handles will be facing down so that you can hang from the pull-up bar through the use of the handles.
2. Once you securely place the V-bar, take a hold of the bar from each side and hang from it. Stick your chest out and lean yourself back slightly in order to better engage the lats. This will be your starting position.
3. Using your lats, pull your torso up while leaning your head back slightly so that you do not hit yourself with the chin-up bar. Continue until your chest nearly touches the V-bar. Exhale as you execute this motion.
4. After a second hold on the contracted position, slowly lower your body back to the starting position as you breathe in.
5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', '["lats"]', '["biceps","upper_back","front_delts"]', '["pull_up_bar"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'v-bar-pullup', 'strength', 'vertical_pull', 'reps_bodyweight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use assistance (band/machine) until you can do clean reps.', 'free_exercise_db', 'V-Bar_Pullup', 'V-Bar Pullup', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=V-Bar+Pull-up+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/V-Bar_Pullup.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '9b1a6360-22d6-5e96-9b01-cca2e1b42960'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
