2. Grip the V-bar with your hands a little wider than your shoulders.
3. Pull the V-bar down to your upper chest, driving your elbows toward your ribs.
4. Let the V-bar rise slowly until your arms are straight.', '["lats"]', '["biceps","upper_back","front_delts"]', '["cable"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'v-bar-pulldown', 'strength', 'vertical_pull', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use assistance (band/machine) until you can do clean reps.', 'free_exercise_db', 'V-Bar_Pulldown', 'V-Bar Pulldown', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=V-Bar+Pulldown+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["csv_disagrees","generic_coaching","media_new_everkinetic_match","no_alternative","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '4e8a72f6-fdb8-5dd6-b021-33bd1ff3ed3b'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('bddefee3-127f-52fa-92a1-b705be120407', 'global', NULL, 'V-Bar Triceps Pushdown', 'v-bar triceps pushdown', 'free_exercise_db', 'An isolation strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the triceps.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Attach a V-Bar to a high pulley and grab with an overhand grip (palms facing down) at shoulder width.
2. Standing upright with the torso straight and a very small inclination forward, bring the upper arms close to your body and perpendicular to the floor. The forearms should be pointing up towards the pulley as they hold the bar. The thumbs should be higher than the small finger. This is your starting position.
3. Using the triceps, bring the bar down until it touches the front of your thighs and the arms are fully extended perpendicular to the floor. The upper arms should always remain stationary next to your torso and only the forearms should move. Exhale as you perform this movement.
4. After a second hold at the contracted position, bring the V-Bar slowly up to the starting point. Breathe in as you perform this step.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["triceps"]', '[]', '["cable"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'triceps-pushdown-v-bar-attachment', 'strength', 'elbow_extension', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Reduce range if you feel elbow pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Triceps_Pushdown_-_V-Bar_Attachment', 'Triceps Pushdown - V-Bar Attachment', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=V-Bar+Triceps+Pushdown+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Triceps_Pushdown_-_V-Bar_Attachment.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","image_match_uncertain","media_match_medium"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'bddefee3-127f-52fa-92a1-b705be120407'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('7ac0875d-59cf-59cc-9da5-27d4283e0a4b', 'global', NULL, 'Wall Sit', 'wall sit', 'library', 'A compound strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the quads, with the glutes and inner thighs assisting.', 'ai_authored:fitbud_curated', '1. Stand with your back flat against a wall and your feet about two feet in front of you.
2. Slide down until your knees are bent to about 90 degrees.
3. Hold the position with your weight in your heels.
4. Push through your heels to slide back up the wall.', '["quads"]', '["glutes","adductors"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'wall-sit', 'strength', 'squat', 'time_hold', 'home', 'compound', 'static', 'bilateral', 'Use safety pins/spotter for heavy barbell work; stop if you feel knee or back pain.', 'fitbud', 'wall_sit', 'Wall sit', 'needs_human', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Wall+Sit+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud"}', 1, 'ai_authored:specific', 1, '["ai_authored_steps","no_drawing","no_image","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '7ac0875d-59cf-59cc-9da5-27d4283e0a4b'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('cc0092e1-fcaa-58ac-b56f-4cd62d9a7c52', 'global', NULL, 'Weighted Pull-up', 'weighted pull-up', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a pull-up bar that mainly works the lats, with the biceps and upper back assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Attach a weight to a dip belt and secure it around your waist. Grab the pull-up bar with the palms of your hands facing forward. For a medium grip, your hands should be spaced at shoulder width. Both arms should be extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip.
2. You''ll want to bring your torso back about 30 degrees while creating a curvature in your lower back and sticking your chest out. This will be your starting position.
3. Now, exhale and pull your torso up until your head is above your hands. Concentrate on squeezing yourshoulder blades back and down as you reach the top contracted position.
4. After a brief moment at the top contracted position, inhale and slowly lower your torso back to the starting position with your arms extended and your lats fully stretched.', '["lats"]', '["biceps","upper_back"]', '["pull_up_bar"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'weighted-pull-ups', 'strength', 'vertical_pull', 'reps_bodyweight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use assistance (band/machine) until you can do clean reps.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Weighted_Pull_Ups', 'Weighted Pull Ups', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Weighted+Pull-up+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Weighted_Pull_Ups.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching","no_alternative"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'cc0092e1-fcaa-58ac-b56f-4cd62d9a7c52'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('eb8fed06-4bd6-5fce-a248-73cb28b1fcd5', 'global', NULL, 'Wide Push-up', 'wide push-up', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using your bodyweight that mainly works the chest, with the abs and front delts assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. With your hands wide apart, support your body on your toes and hands in a plank position. Your elbows should be extended and your body straight. Do not allow your hips to sag. This will be your starting position.
2. To begin, allow the elbows to flex, lowering your chest to the floor as you inhale.
3. Using your pectoral muscles, press your upper body back up to the starting position by extending the elbows. Exhale as you perform this step.
4. After pausing at the contracted position, repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', '["chest"]', '["abs","front_delts","triceps"]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'push-up-wide', 'strength', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'compound', NULL, 'bilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Push-Up_Wide', 'Push-Up Wide', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Wide+Push-up+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Push-Up_Wide.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 1, '["generic_coaching","media_variant_drawing","no_image"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'eb8fed06-4bd6-5fce-a248-73cb28b1fcd5'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('577bc835-2fab-5966-a447-75e1a1eb0638', 'global', NULL, 'Wide Stance Barbell Squat', 'wide stance barbell squat', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a barbell that mainly works the quads, with the calves and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.
3. Step away from the rack and position your legs using a wider-than-shoulder-width stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up at all times as looking down will get you off balance, and also maintain a straight back. This will be your starting position.
4. Begin to slowly lower the bar by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calves becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to the floor). Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. If your knees are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the starting position.
6. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["quads"]', '["calves","glutes","hamstrings","lower_back"]', '["barbell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'wide-stance-barbell-squat', 'strength', 'squat', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use safety pins/spotter for heavy barbell work; stop if you feel knee or back pain.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Wide_Stance_Barbell_Squat', 'Wide Stance Barbell Squat', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Wide+Stance+Barbell+Squat+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Wide_Stance_Barbell_Squat.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '577bc835-2fab-5966-a447-75e1a1eb0638'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('92da84d7-f61c-50a9-9bf3-de77fd6bc346', 'global', NULL, 'Wide-Grip Barbell Bench Press', 'wide-grip barbell bench press', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a barbell that mainly works the chest, with the front delts and triceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Lie back on a flat bench with feet firm on the floor. Using a wide, pronated (palms forward) grip that is around 3 inches away from shoulder width (for each hand), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with your arms locked. The bar will be perpendicular to the torso and the floor. This will be your starting position.
2. As you breathe in, come down slowly until you feel the bar on your middle chest.
3. After a second pause, bring the bar back to the starting position as you breathe out and push the bar using your chest muscles. Lock your arms and squeeze your chest in the contracted position, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly again.
4. Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', '["chest"]', '["front_delts","triceps"]', '["barbell","bench"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'wide-grip-barbell-bench-press', 'strength', 'horizontal_push', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Use a spotter or safety arms for heavy pressing.', 'free_exercise_db', 'Wide-Grip_Barbell_Bench_Press', 'Wide-Grip Barbell Bench Press', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Wide-Grip+Barbell+Bench+Press+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Wide-Grip_Barbell_Bench_Press.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_authored:pattern', 0, '["generic_coaching"]', 'library+csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '92da84d7-f61c-50a9-9bf3-de77fd6bc346'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
