3. Rise as high as you can onto the balls of your feet.
4. Pause for a second at the top, then lower slowly.
5. Finish all reps on one leg, then switch legs.', '["calves"]', '[]', '["dumbbell","bench"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'one-leg-seated-dumbbell-calf-raise', 'strength', 'calf_raise', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'isolation', 'push', 'unilateral', 'Hold a support for balance.', 'user_csv', 'user_exercises.csv:703', 'One-Leg Seated Dumbbell Calf Raise', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dumbbell+Seated+Single-Leg+Calf+Raise+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud","replaces":"free_exercise_db"}', 1, 'ai_derived:pattern', 1, '["steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '01290da9-04ac-5203-a1cb-ee011a74fa6f'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('65618d9c-1129-5457-988a-6c9b67a0e876', 'global', NULL, 'Dumbbell Single-Arm Upright Row', 'dumbbell single-arm upright row', 'free_exercise_db', 'A single-side compound strength exercise using dumbbells that mainly works the traps, with the biceps assisting.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Grab a dumbbell and stand up straight with your arm extended in front of you with a slight bend at the elbows and your back straight. This will be your starting position.
2. Keep the other hand can be kept fully extended to the side, by the waist or grabbing a fixed surface. This will be your starting position.
3. Use your side shoulders to lift the dumbbell as you exhale. The dumbbell should be close to the body as you move it up. Continue to lift it until the dumbbell is nearly in line with your chin. As you lift the dumbbell, your elbow should always be higher than your forearm. Also, keep your torso stationary and pause for a second at the top of the movement.
4. Lower the dumbbell back down slowly to the starting position. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and switch arms.', '["traps"]', '["biceps"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'one-arm-dumbbell-upright-row', 'strength', 'shoulder_isolation', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'compound', 'pull', 'unilateral', 'Use light loads; these are accessory movements.', 'user_csv', 'user_exercises.csv:663', 'One-Arm Dumbbell Upright Row', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dumbbell+Single-Arm+Upright+Row+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Dumbbell_One-Arm_Upright_Row.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_derived:pattern', 0, '[]', 'csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '65618d9c-1129-5457-988a-6c9b67a0e876'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('00b68928-b4b9-5793-957f-293f54f838fe', 'global', NULL, 'Dumbbell Single-Leg Hip Thrust', 'dumbbell single-leg hip thrust', 'wger', 'A single-side isolation strength exercise with dumbbells that mainly works the glutes, with the abs and hamstrings assisting.', 'ai_authored:fitbud_curated', '1. Sit on the floor with your upper back against a bench and knees bent, feet flat.
2. Rest the dumbbells across your hips.
3. Lift one foot off the floor.
4. Drive through your heels to lift your hips until your body is straight from shoulders to knees.
5. Squeeze your glutes at the top, then lower your hips slowly.
6. Finish all reps on one leg, then switch legs.', '["glutes"]', '["abs","hamstrings"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'single-leg-hip-thrust-with-dumbbell', 'strength', 'hinge', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'isolation', 'pull', 'unilateral', 'Start light; stop if you feel sharp lower-back pain.', 'user_csv', 'user_exercises.csv:945', 'Single Leg Hip Thrust with Dumbbell', 'approve_with_flags', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dumbbell+Single-Leg+Hip+Thrust+exercise+form', 'fitbud_written', '{"licence":"FitBud proprietary (own wording)","author":"FitBud"}', 1, 'ai_derived:pattern', 1, '["no_drawing","steps_fitbud_written_trainer_review"]', 'csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '00b68928-b4b9-5793-957f-293f54f838fe'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('5008d1ba-6088-5403-9981-94efe1b7378e', 'global', NULL, 'Dumbbell Split Squat with Jump', 'dumbbell split squat with jump', 'user_csv', 'A single-side compound strength exercise with dumbbells that mainly works the quads, with the calves and glutes assisting.', 'ai_authored:fitbud_curated', '1. Hold the dumbbells at your sides.
2. Take a long split stance with your back heel lifted.
3. Lower your back knee straight down toward the floor until your front thigh is about parallel.
