3. Without moving your upper arms or shoulders, bend your elbows and flare them outward to the sides. Lower the inner ends of the dumbbells toward the center of your chest.
4. Gently touch the dumbbells to your chest. Do not rest the weight on your body; maintain constant tension in your triceps.
5. Forcefully extend your elbows to return the dumbbells to the starting position. Focus on "pushing your pinkies toward the sky" to maximize triceps engagement.', '["triceps"]', '[]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'dumbbell-tate-press', 'strength', 'elbow_extension', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Reduce range if you feel elbow pain.', 'user_csv', 'user_exercises.csv:353', 'Dumbbell Tate Press', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dumbbell+Tate+Press+exercise+form', 'wger', '{"licence":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","source_url":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1824/view/","author":"beagle","modified":"HTML list converted to ordered steps; curated edit to pass step validation (curation/steps_source_fixes.tsv)","share_alike":true}', 0, 'ai_derived:pattern', 0, '[]', 'csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'b60bd338-1b50-5da1-a7ab-f88cd0ae0797'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
