2. Extend your arms above you with a slight bend at the elbows.
3. Now rotate the wrists so that the palms of your hands are facing you. This will be your starting position.
4. As you breathe in, start to slowly lower the arms to the side while keeping the arms extended and while rotating the wrists until the palms of the hand are facing each other.
5. As you exhale start to bring the dumbbells back up to the starting position by reversing the motion and rotating the hands so that the pinky fingers are next to each other again. There is no motion that happens at the elbow joint.
6. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["chest"]', '["shoulders","triceps"]', '["dumbbell","bench"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'incline-dumbbell-twist-fly', 'strength', 'chest_fly', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'isolation', 'push', 'bilateral', 'Stop short of shoulder discomfort at the bottom.', 'user_csv', 'user_exercises.csv:493', 'Incline Dumbbell Twist Fly', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Incline+Dumbbell+Twist+Fly+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Flyes_-_With_A_Twist.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_derived:pattern', 1, '["media_variant_drawing"]', 'csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = 'ff0b35f7-b66a-5e2a-ae8c-932cc1eba4bf'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
