2. Keep your feet flat on the floor and stretch your arms overhead with your palms crossed. This will be your starting position.
3. Curl your upper body forward and bring your shoulder blades just off the floor. At all times, keep your arms aligned with your head, neck and shoulder. Don''t move them forward from that position. Exhale as you perform this portion of the movement and hold the contraction for a second.
4. Slowly lower down to the starting position as you inhale.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["bodyweight"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'hands-overhead-ab-crunch', 'strength', 'core_flexion', 'reps_bodyweight', 'home', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Skip or modify if it aggravates lower-back pain.', 'user_csv', 'user_exercises.csv:462', 'Hands Overhead Ab Crunch', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Overhead-Reach+Crunch+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Crunch_-_Hands_Overhead.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_derived:pattern', 0, '["no_drawing"]', 'csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '5c609ffa-771c-59bb-9be1-6af54025dfa2'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO `exercise_library_items` (`id`, `ownership`, `trainer_user_id`, `name`, `name_norm`, `name_source`, `description`, `description_provenance`, `instructions`, `primary_muscles_json`, `secondary_muscles_json`, `equipment_json`, `difficulty`, `status`, `slug`, `category_code`, `movement_pattern_code`, `logging_type_code`, `setting`, `mechanic`, `force`, `laterality`, `safety_note`, `source_id`, `source_ref`, `source_name`, `review_status`, `youtube_search_url`, `steps_source`, `steps_licence_json`, `steps_review_required`, `coaching_provenance`, `needs_human_review`, `review_flags_json`, `origin`, `seed_version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('8b2844d0-fc34-574c-aab3-e6b745b5247b', 'global', NULL, 'Pallof Press with Rotation', 'pallof press with rotation', 'free_exercise_db', 'A compound strength exercise using a cable station that mainly works the abs.', 'ai_authored:facts_template', '1. Connect a standard handle to a tower, and position the cable to shoulder height. With your side to the cable, grab the handle with one hand and step away from the tower. You should be approximately arm''s length away from the pulley, with the tension of the weight on the cable. Align outstretched arm with cable.
2. With your feet positioned hip-width apart, pull the cable into your chest and grab the handle with your other hand. Both hands should be on the handle at this time.
3. Facing forward, press the cable away from your chest. You core should be tight and engaged.
4. Keeping your hips straight, twist your torso away from the pulley until you get a full quarter rotation. Maintain your rigid stance and straight arms. Return to the neutral position in a slow and controlled manner. Your arms should be extended in front of you.
5. With the side tension still engaging your core, bring your hands to your chest and immediately press outward to a fully extended position. This constitutes one rep. Repeat to failure.
6. Then, reposition and repeat the same series of movements on the opposite side.', '["abs"]', '[]', '["cable"]', 'intermediate', 'active', 'pallof-press-with-rotation', 'strength', 'core_anti_extension', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'static', 'bilateral', 'Stop when form breaks rather than chasing time.', 'user_csv', 'user_exercises.csv:719', 'Pallof Press with Rotation', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Pallof+Press+with+Rotation+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Pallof_Press_With_Rotation.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_derived:pattern', 0, '["no_drawing"]', 'csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '8b2844d0-fc34-574c-aab3-e6b745b5247b'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
