2. Grip the bar with your hands just outside shoulder-width, set your shoulder blades back and down, and lift it out of the rack to straight arms over your shoulders.
3. Lower the bar until it rests briefly on the safety pins set just above your chest.
4. Press the bar back up to straight arms, keeping your feet planted and your upper back tight.
