2. Lift the barbell up and fully extend your arms with your back straight. There should be a slight bend at the elbows. This is the starting position.
3. Use your side shoulders to lift the bar as you exhale. The bar should be close to the body as you move it up. Continue to lift it until it nearly touches your chin. As you lift the bar, your elbows should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torso stationary and pause for a second at the top of the movement.
4. Lower the bar back down slowly to the starting position. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.
5. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["side_delts"]', '["traps"]', '["smith_machine"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'smith-machine-upright-row', 'strength', 'shoulder_isolation', 'reps_weight', 'gym', 'compound', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use light loads; these are accessory movements.', 'user_csv', 'user_exercises.csv:992', 'Smith Machine Upright Row', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Smith+Machine+Upright+Row+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Smith_Machine_Upright_Row.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_derived:pattern', 0, '[]', 'csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '725831c3-5530-5085-8e98-104c9d570873'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
