3. Slowly begin to bring the dumbbells back to starting position as your breathe in.
4. Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.', '["biceps"]', '["forearms"]', '["dumbbell"]', 'beginner', 'active', 'standing-dumbbell-reverse-curl', 'strength', 'elbow_flexion', 'reps_weight', 'both', 'isolation', 'pull', 'bilateral', 'Use a load you can control for the whole set.', 'user_csv', 'user_exercises.csv:1039', 'Standing Dumbbell Reverse Curl', 'approve', 'https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Standing+Dumbbell+Reverse+Curl+exercise+form', 'free_exercise_db', '{"licence":"Unlicense","licence_url":"https://unlicense.org/","source_url":"https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db (exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Reverse_Curl.json)","author":"free-exercise-db contributors","modified":"split/merged into 3-6 ordered steps; non-instruction sentences removed"}', 0, 'ai_derived:pattern', 0, '["no_drawing"]', 'csv', '2026.10.21-v3', COALESCE((SELECT `created_at` FROM `exercise_library_items` WHERE `id` = '0a6fb701-286b-5ee3-a2ad-3d27c6bd07c7'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z'), '2026-10-20T18:30:00.000Z');
